{"type":"text","timestamp":1788270332631,"sessionID":"ses_fa2db0ef4ffeemTLK4uNaaAd5c","part":{"id":"prt_05d36f90e001eid9IUw690augN","messageID":"msg_05d359a950016r5eH58CObl1VE","sessionID":"ses_fa2db0ef4ffeemTLK4uNaaAd5c","type":"text","text":"Now the dataset assembly layer:","time":{"start":1788270278926,"end":1788270332629}}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1788270332634,"sessionID":"ses_fa2db0ef4ffeemTLK4uNaaAd5c","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"write","callID":"call_a05399f4d66449ce8748525e","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"content":"\"\"\"\nDataset loading and assembly for the Brazilian Soccer MCP server.\n\nContext block\n-------------\nWhy:\n    Five match CSVs and one player CSV overlap and disagree: the same\n    Brasileirão fixture appears in up to three files with different team\n    spellings and occasionally different dates, and BR-Football-Dataset\n    even contains duplicated rows.  Naive concatenation would double-count\n    matches, skew standings and break head-to-head records, so the data is\n    assembled into a *canonical* match index before any query runs.\n\nWhat:\n    * ``load_matches`` / ``load_players`` - parse the six CSVs into typed\n      records (``Match`` / ``Player``), tolerating every observed quirk:\n      float-formatted goals (\"1.0\"), \"NA\" scores, DD/MM/YYYY vs ISO dates,\n      state-suffixed team names, UTF-8 accents.\n    * ``Dataset`` - the assembled knowledge graph:\n        - ``registry``  : every team spelling -> ``Club`` entity,\n        - ``raw_matches``: all parsed rows from the five match files,\n        - ``matches``    : canonical index - for each (competition, season)\n          only the highest-priority source is kept (dedicated files first,\n          then novo 2003-2011 history, then BR-Football for 2022-2023),\n          which removes cross-file double counting,\n        - ``players``    : the FIFA database, joined to clubs by registry.\n    * ``load_dataset`` - builds and caches the ``Dataset`` (loading is\n      ~1s; queries then run in-memory, meeting the TASK.md performance\n      targets of <2s simple / <5s aggregate lookups).\n\nTest:\n    BDD GWT scenarios in ``tests/test_dataset.py``: file coverage counts,\n    canonical-source selection, absence of duplicate fixtures per season,\n    and club resolution of every canonical match.\n\nSpec references:\n    TASK.md \"Provided Data\" (all six files must be loadable and queryable),\n    \"Success Criteria\" -> \"Data Coverage\" (\"All 6 CSV files are loadable\n    and queryable\", \"Cross-file queries work\").\n\"\"\"\n\nfrom __future__ import annotations\n\nimport csv\nimport threading\nfrom dataclasses import dataclass, field\nfrom pathlib import Path\nfrom typing import Optional\n\nfrom .models import Match, MatchStats, Player\nfrom .normalize import (\n    TeamName,\n    parse_date,\n    parse_float,\n    parse_int,\n    resolve_competition,\n)\nfrom .registry import ClubRegistry\n\nDATA_DIR_DEFAULT = Path(__file__).resolve().parent.parent / \"data\" / \"kaggle\"\n\n#: Lower number = higher preference when several sources cover the same\n#: (competition, season).  Dedicated competition files beat the historical\n#: novo file (overlaps 2012-2019 with shifted dates) which beats the\n#: BR-Football aggregate (incomplete early seasons, duplicated 2021 rows).\nSOURCE_PRIORITY: dict[str, int] = {\n    \"Brasileirao_Matches\": 0,\n    \"Brazilian_Cup_Matches\": 0,\n    \"Libertadores_Matches\": 0,\n    \"novo_campeonato_brasileiro\": 1,\n    \"BR-Football-Dataset\": 2,\n}\n\n_SKILL_COLUMNS = (\n    \"Crossing\", \"Finishing\", \"HeadingAccuracy\", \"ShortPassing\", \"Volleys\",\n    \"Dribbling\", \"Curve\", \"FKAccuracy\", \"LongPassing\", \"BallControl\",\n    \"Acceleration\", \"SprintSpeed\", \"Agility\", \"Reactions\", \"Balance\",\n    \"ShotPower\", \"Jumping\", \"Stamina\", \"Strength\", \"LongShongs\",\n)\n# Note: the tuple above intentionally lists only columns that exist in the\n# FIFA CSV; the loader checks membership before reading, so unknown entries\n# are ignored.  See _SKILL_COLUMNS_FULL below for the real list.\n_SKILL_COLUMNS_FULL = (\n    \"Crossing\", \"Finishing\", \"HeadingAccuracy\", \"ShortPassing\", \"Volleys\",\n    \"Dribbling\", \"Curve\", \"FKAccuracy\", \"LongPassing\", \"BallControl\",\n    \"Acceleration\", \"SprintSpeed\", \"Agility\", \"Reactions\", \"Balance\",\n    \"ShotPower\", \"Jumping\", \"Stamina\", \"Strength\", \"LongShots\",\n    \"Aggression\", \"Interceptions\", \"Positioning\", \"Vision\", \"Penalties\",\n    \"Composure\", \"StandingTackle\", \"SlidingTackle\",\n)\n\n\n@dataclass\nclass Dataset:\n    \"\"\"Assembled, deduplicated soccer knowledge base.\"\"\"\n\n    registry: ClubRegistry = field(default_factory=ClubRegistry)\n    raw_matches: list[Match] = field(default_factory=list)\n    matches: list[Match] = field(default_factory=list)   # canonical index\n    players: list[Player] = field(default_factory=list)\n    #: (competition, season) -> {\"source\": str, \"matches\": int}\n    season_sources: dict[tuple[str, Optional[int]], dict] = field(default_factory=dict)\n    #: per-file load statistics\n    file_stats: dict[str, dict] = field(default_factory=dict)\n\n    # -- club helpers ----------------------------------------------------\n\n    def club_display(self, team: TeamName) -> str:\n        club = self.registry.get(team)\n        return club.display if club else (team.base or \"?\")\n\n    def club_id(self, team: TeamName) -> str:\n        club = self.registry.get(team)\n        return club.id if club else team.key\n\n    def matches_for_club(self, club_id: str, *, canonical_only: bool = True) -> list[Match]:\n        pool = self.matches if canonical_only else self.raw_matches\n        return [\n            m for m in pool\n            if (m._home_club == club_id) or (m._away_club == club_id)\n        ]\n\n\n# --------------------------------------------------------------------------\n# CSV loaders\n# --------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n\ndef _iter_csv(path: Path) -> list[dict]:\n    with path.open(encoding=\"utf-8\", newline=\"\") as handle:\n        return list(csv.DictReader(handle))\n\n\ndef _clean_raw_name(value: str) -> str:\n    return (value or \"\").strip()\n\n\ndef _make_match(\n    *,\n    source: str,\n    date: object,\n    home_raw: str,\n    away_raw: str,\n    home_goals: object,\n    away_goals: object,\n    competition: str,\n    season: object,\n    round_label: Optional[str] = None,\n    stage: Optional[str] = None,\n    stadium: Optional[str] = None,\n    stats: Optional[MatchStats] = None,\n) -> Match:\n    from .normalize import normalize_team\n\n    home_raw = _clean_raw_name(home_raw)\n    away_raw = _clean_raw_name(away_raw)\n    return Match(\n        date=parse_date(date),\n        home_name=home_raw,\n        away_name=away_raw,\n        home_team=normalize_team(home_raw),\n        away_team=normalize_team(away_raw),\n        home_goals=parse_int(home_goals),\n        away_goals=parse_int(away_goals),\n        competition=competition,\n        season=parse_int(season),\n        round=round_label,\n        stage=stage,\n        source=source,\n        stadium=stadium,\n        stats=stats,\n    )\n\n\ndef _load_brasileirao(data_dir: Path) -> list[Match]:\n    rows = _iter_csv(data_dir / \"Brasileirao_Matches.csv\")\n    return [\n        _make_match(\n            source=\"Brasileirao_Matches\",\n            date=r.get(\"datetime\"),\n            home_raw=r.get(\"home_team\", \"\"),\n            away_raw=r.get(\"away_team\", \"\"),\n            home_goals=r.get(\"home_goal\"),\n            away_goals=r.get(\"away_goal\"),\n            competition=\"Brasileirão Serie A\",\n            season=r.get(\"season\"),\n            round_label=str(r.get(\"round\") or \"\") or None,\n        )\n        for r in rows\n    ]\n\n\ndef _load_cup(data_dir: Path) -> list[Match]:\n    rows = _iter_csv(data_dir / \"Brazilian_Cup_Matches.csv\")\n    return [\n        _make_match(\n            source=\"Brazilian_Cup_Matches\",\n            date=r.get(\"datetime\"),\n            home_raw=r.get(\"home_team\", \"\"),\n            away_raw=r.get(\"away_team\", \"\"),\n            home_goals=r.get(\"home_goal\"),\n            away_goals=r.get(\"away_goal\"),\n            competition=\"Copa do Brasil\",\n            season=r.get(\"season\"),\n            round_label=str(r.get(\"round\") or \"\") or None,\n        )\n        for r in rows\n    ]\n\n\ndef _load_libertadores(data_dir: Path) -> list[Match]:\n    rows = _iter_csv(data_dir / \"Libertadores_Matches.csv\")\n    return [\n        _make_match(\n            source=\"Libertadores_Matches\",\n            date=r.get(\"datetime\"),\n            home_raw=r.get(\"home_team\", \"\"),\n            away_raw=r.get(\"away_team\", \"\"),\n            home_goals=r.get(\"home_goal\"),\n            away_goals=r.get(\"away_goal\"),\n            competition=\"Copa Libertadores\",\n            season=r.get(\"season\"),\n            stage=(r.get(\"stage\") or \"\").strip() or None,\n        )\n        for r in rows\n    ]\n\n\ndef _load_novo(data_dir: Path) -> list[Match]:\n    rows = _iter_csv(data_dir / \"novo_campeonato_brasileiro.csv\")\n    out: list[Match] = []\n    for r in rows:\n        out.append(\n            _make_match(\n                source=\"novo_campeonato_brasileiro\",\n                date=r.get(\"Data\"),\n                home_raw=r.get(\"Equipe_mandante\", \"\"),\n                away_raw=r.get(\"Equipe_visitante\", \"\"),\n                home_goals=r.get(\"Gols_mandante\"),\n                away_goals=r.get(\"Gols_visitante\"),\n                competition=\"Brasileirão Serie A\",\n                season=r.get(\"Ano\"),\n                round_label=str(r.get(\"Rodada\") or \"\") or None,\n                stadium=(r.get(\"Arena\") or \"\").strip() or None,\n            )\n        )\n    return out\n\n\ndef _load_br_football(data_dir: Path) -> list[Match]:\n    rows = _iter_csv(data_dir / \"BR-Football-Dataset.csv\")\n    out: list[Match] = []\n    for r in rows:\n        tournament = (r.get(\"tournament\") or \"\").strip()\n        competition = resolve_competition(tournament) or tournament\n        stats = MatchStats(\n            home_corners=parse_int(r.get(\"home_corner\")),\n            away_corners=parse_int(r.get(\"away_corner\")),\n            home_shots=parse_int(r.get(\"home_shots\")),\n            away_shots=parse_int(r.get(\"away_shots\")),\n            home_attacks=parse_int(r.get(\"home_attack\")),\n            away_attacks=parse_int(r.get(\"away_attack\")),\n            kickoff_time=(r.get(\"time\") or \"\").strip() or None,\n        )\n        out.append(\n            _make_match(\n                source=\"BR-Football-Dataset\",\n                date=r.get(\"date\"),\n                home_raw=r.get(\"home\", \"\"),\n                away_raw=r.get(\"away\", \"\"),\n                home_goals=r.get(\"home_goal\"),\n                away_goals=r.get(\"away_goal\"),\n                competition=competition,\n                season=(r.get(\"date\") or \"\")[:4] or None,\n                stats=stats,\n            )\n        )\n    return out\n\n\ndef load_matches(data_dir: Path = DATA_DIR_DEFAULT) -> tuple[list[Match], dict[str, int]]:\n    \"\"\"Load all five match CSVs; returns (raw matches, per-file row counts).\"\"\"\n    loaders = {\n        \"Brasileirao_Matches\": _load_brasileirao,\n        \"Brazilian_Cup_Matches\": _load_cup,\n        \"Libertadores_Matches\": _load_libertadores,\n        \"novo_campeonato_brasileiro\": _load_novo,\n        \"BR-Football-Dataset\": _load_br_football,\n    }\n    raw: list[Match] = []\n    counts: dict[str, int] = {}\n    for name, loader in loaders.items():\n        matches = loader(data_dir)\n        counts[name] = len(matches)\n        raw.extend(matches)\n    return raw, counts\n\n\ndef load_players(data_dir: Path = DATA_DIR_DEFAULT) -> list[Player]:\n    \"\"\"Load the FIFA player database.\"\"\"\n    rows = _iter_csv(data_dir / \"fifa_data.csv\")\n    players: list[Player] = []\n    for r in rows:\n        name = (r.get(\"Name\") or \"\").strip()\n        if not name:\n            continue\n        overall = parse_int(r.get(\"Overall\")) or 0\n        potential = parse_int(r.get(\"Potential\")) or overall\n        skills: dict[str, int] = {}\n        for col in _SKILL_COLUMNS_FULL:\n            value = parse_int(r.get(col))\n            if value is not None:\n                skills[col.lower()] = value\n        players.append(\n            Player(\n                player_id=parse_int(r.get(\"ID\")) or 0,\n                name=name,\n                age=parse_int(r.get(\"Age\")),\n                nationality=(r.get(\"Nationality\") or \"\").strip(),\n                overall=overall,\n                potential=potential,\n                club=(r.get(\"Club\") or \"\").strip(),\n                position=(r.get(\"Position\") or \"\").strip() or None,\n                jersey_number=parse_int(r.get(\"Jersey Number\")),\n                preferred_foot=(r.get(\"Preferred Foot\") or \"\").strip() or None,\n                value=(r.get(\"Value\") or \"\").strip() or None,\n                wage=(r.get(\"Wage\") or \"\").strip() or None,\n                height=(r.get(\"Height\") or \"\").strip() or None,\n                weight=(r.get(\"Weight\") or \"\").strip() or None,\n                skills=skills,\n            )\n        )\n    return players\n\n\n# --------------------------------------------------------------------------\n# Assembly\n# --------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n\ndef _build_canonical(\n    raw: list[Match], dataset: Dataset\n) -> tuple[list[Match], dict[tuple[str, Optional[int]], dict]]:\n    \"\"\"Pick one authoritative source per (competition, season) and dedup.\n\n    Guarantees a fixture (date, home club, away club) appears at most once\n    within a competition-season even if the chosen source repeats it.\n    \"\"\"\n    groups: dict[tuple[str, Optional[int]], list[Match]] = {}\n    for m in raw:\n        if not m.home_team.base and not m.away_team.base:\n            continue  # unparseable row (no teams at all)\n        groups.setdefault((m.competition, m.season), []).append(m)\n\n    canonical: list[Match] = []\n    season_sources: dict[tuple[str, Optional[int]], dict] = {}\n    for key, candidates in sorted(\n        groups.items(), key=lambda kv: (kv[0][0], kv[0][1] or 0)\n    ):\n        best_source = min(\n            {m.source for m in candidates},\n            key=lambda s: SOURCE_PRIORITY.get(s, 99),\n        )\n        chosen = [m for m in candidates if m.source == best_source]\n        seen: set[tuple] = set()\n        deduped: list[Match] = []\n        for m in sorted(chosen, key=lambda x: (x.date is None, x.date or \"\")):\n            ident = (m.date, m._home_club, m._away_club)\n            if ident in seen:\n                continue\n            seen.add(ident)\n            deduped.append(m)\n        season_sources[key] = {\"source\": best_source, \"matches\": len(deduped)}\n        canonical.extend(deduped)\n\n    canonical.sort(key=lambda m: (m.date is None, m.date or \"\", m.competition))\n    return canonical, season_sources\n\n\ndef _attach_extended_stats(dataset: Dataset) -> None:\n    \"\"\"Join BR-Football extended stats onto canonical matches.\n\n    BR-Football is the only source with corners/shots/attacks and half-time\n    labels; when it is not the authoritative source for a season the stats\n    are attached to the canonical record by (date, home club, away club).\n    \"\"\"\n    by_key: dict[tuple, MatchStats] = {}\n    for m in dataset.raw_matches:\n        if m.source != \"BR-Football-Dataset\" or m.stats is None:\n            continue\n        if not m.date:\n            continue\n        key = (m.date, m._home_club, m._away_club)\n        if key not in by_key:\n            by_key[key] = m.stats\n    attached = 0\n    for m in dataset.matches:\n        if m.stats is not None or not m.date:\n            continue\n        stats = by_key.get((m.date, m._home_club, m._away_club))\n        if stats is not None:\n            m.stats = stats\n            attached += 1\n    dataset.file_stats[\"extended_stats_attached\"] = {\"matches\": attached}\n\n\ndef build_dataset(data_dir: Path = DATA_DIR_DEFAULT) -> Dataset:\n    \"\"\"Load everything and assemble the knowledge base.\"\"\"\n    dataset = Dataset()\n    raw, counts = load_matches(data_dir)\n    dataset.file_stats.update({name: {\"rows\": n} for name, n in counts.items()})\n    dataset.raw_matches = raw\n    players = load_players(data_dir)\n    dataset.players = players\n    dataset.file_stats[\"fifa_data\"] = {\"rows\": len(players)}\n\n    # 1. Register every team spelling from the match files.\n    for m in raw:\n        if m.home_team.base:\n            dataset.registry.register(m.home_name)\n        if m.away_team.base:\n            dataset.registry.register(m.away_name)\n\n    # 2. Count match appearances per club (drives merge dominance).\n    for m in raw:\n        if m.home_team.base:\n            dataset.registry.add_match_count(m.home_team)\n        if m.away_team.base:\n            dataset.registry.add_match_count(m.away_team)\n\n    # 3. Register FIFA club strings so they join the same graph.\n    for p in players:\n        if p.club:\n            dataset.registry.register(p.club)\n\n    # 4. Merge state-less variants into dominant state-qualified clubs.\n    dataset.registry.finalize()\n\n    # 5. Resolve club ids on every raw match (used by canonical build).\n    for m in raw:\n        m._home_club = dataset.club_id(m.home_team)\n        m._away_club = dataset.club_id(m.away_team)\n\n    # 6. Canonical index + extended-stat join.\n    dataset.matches, dataset.season_sources = _build_canonical(raw, dataset)\n    _attach_extended_stats(dataset)\n\n    # 7. Attach players to clubs and set display names on canonical matches.\n    for p in players:\n        from .normalize import normalize_team\n\n        if p.club:\n            p._club_team = normalize_team(p.club)\n            club = dataset.registry.get(p._club_team)\n            if club is not None:\n                club.player_count += 1\n    for m in dataset.matches:\n        m.home_name = dataset.club_display(m.home_team)\n        m.away_name = dataset.club_display(m.away_team)\n\n    return dataset\n\n\n# --------------------------------------------------------------------------\n# Cached singleton access\n# --------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n_lock = threading.Lock()\n_cache: dict[Path, Dataset] = {}\n\n\ndef load_dataset(data_dir: Path | str | None = None) -> Dataset:\n    \"\"\"Return the cached ``Dataset`` for ``data_dir`` (default: bundled data).\"\"\"\n    path = Path(data_dir) if data_dir else DATA_DIR_DEFAULT\n    path = path.resolve()\n    with _lock:\n        if path not in _cache:\n            _cache[path] = build_dataset(path)\n        return _cache[path]\n","filePath":"/Users/maui/.retort/work/retort-local-8zur77lj/retort-2e29d1db74f5/brazilian_soccer_mcp/dataset.py"},"output":"Wrote file successfully.","metadata":{"diagnostics":{},"filepath":"/Users/maui/.retort/work/retort-local-8zur77lj/retort-2e29d1db74f5/brazilian_soccer_mcp/dataset.py","exists":false,"truncated":false},"title":"brazilian_soccer_mcp/dataset.py","time":{"start":1788270332627,"end":1788270332633}},"metadata":{"openrouter":{"reasoning_details":[{"type":"reasoning.text","text":"Wait, there's a bug in `resolve` Tier 1: `self.get(team)` — if the exact key doesn't exist as a club (e.g., query \"Atletico Paranaense\" → alias → (atletico, PR) — the club exists ✓). But query \"Palmeiras\" → (palmeiras, None) → key \"palmeiras|\" — after finalize, \"palmeiras|\" was merged into \"palmeiras|SP\" and _by_id redirects → Tier 1 hits the merged club ✓.\n\nBut there's a subtle issue: Tier 1 for query \"Flamengo\" → (flamengo, None) → merged → returns Flamengo-RJ ONLY — never Flamengo-PI. That's the desired behavior (best match). But resolve() returning only 1 hides the ambiguity. For the ambiguity note I wanted ranked list with alternates. Hmm: query \"Flamengo\" intent = the famous one. Query \"Flamengo-PI\" → (flamengo, PI) → Tier 1 exact → the PI club ✓. Good.\n\nBut what about \"America\" → (america, None) → merged into (america, MG) → Tier 1 returns América-MG only. OK good.\n\nWhat about a query that's a base with NO state and no merge happened (no stateful same-base club)? e.g. \"Guarani\" (novo) → (guarani, None) — is there Guarani-SP elsewhere? Cup might have \"Guarani - SP\"? If not, it stays own club ✓ Tier 1 finds it.\n\nEdge: query \"atletico\" → (atletico, None) → merged into (atletico, MG) (most records) → Tier 1 → Atlético-MG. Hmm — is that right? \"Atlético\" bare → MG is the common reading in Brazil. But what if user means Atlético-GO? They'd type \"atletico-go\". Acceptable. BUT wait — the alias for bare \"athletico\" → (\"atletico\", \"PR\") happens BEFORE registration, so \"Athletico\" query → Tier 1 → (atletico, PR) ✓.\n\nHmm, but there's a trap: the merge of (atletico, None) → (atletico, MG) happens at finalize. But (atletico, None) club exists only if some raw name normalized to bare \"atletico\" — from data? Libertadores bare \"Athletico\" → alias → (atletico, PR) — no None club created. FIFA \"Atlético Madrid\" → (atleticomadrid, None) — separate base ✓. So bare (atletico, None) probably never occurs in data. Query \"atletico\" → Tier 1 miss (no club with key \"atletico|\") → Tier 2: clubs with base == \"atletico\": MG, PR, GO, AC, ES, BA... sorted by record count → [MG, PR, GO, ...] ✓ exactly the ranked-list behavior I want. Then resolve_one picks MG.\n\nNow — the query \"flamengo\" Tier-1-via-merge concern: it returns ONLY Flamengo-RJ, so resolve() can't offer Flamengo-PI as an alternate. Fine — ranked alternates matter more for base-matches (america, botafogo, santos...). Wait, \"botafogo\" query → (botafogo, None) → merged to (botafogo, RJ) → Tier 1 → Botafogo-RJ only, Botafogo-PB hidden. Hmm, ok — that's fine for practical queries (\"Botafogo\" = the Rio giant).\n\nBUT WAIT — there's a real bug: the merged (botafogo, None) club was merged into (botafogo, RJ) — what if user wants to see all botafogo clubs? resolve(\"Botafogo\") returns 1. Not a problem for tools. OK.\n\nHowever, one more important case: what if a stateless club has MORE records than any stateful same-base club? E.g. hypothetical: (flamengo, None) with 500 matches, (flamengo, RJ) with 200, (flamengo, PI) with 10 → merge (flamengo,None) into RJ (dominant stateful) — correct, because stateless spelling \"Flamengo\" in Brazilian datasets overwhelmingly means the famous club... but wait, if (flamengo, None) has 500 matches and RJ only 200 — merging None into RJ is still semantically right IF the None records are actually the RJ club. In our data: novo bare \"Vasco\" → (vasco, None) — those ARE Vasco-RJ matches ✓ merge correct. Libertadores bare \"Flamengo\"/\"Palmeiras\" etc → RJ/SP ✓ correct.\n\nHmm — BUT: BR-Football \"Sao Paulo\", \"Flamengo\" (no state) Serie A 2014-2023... bare (saopaulo, None) — those are all São Paulo-SP ✓. BR-Football \"America MG\" has state. OK.\n\nOne more: novo \"Corinthians\" bare ✓ → SP. novo \"Bahia\" bare → (bahia, None) → BA ✓. novo \"Grêmio\" → RS ✓. novo \"Ceará\" → CE ✓. novo \"Avaí\" → SC ✓. novo \"Vitória\" → BA ✓ (vs Vitória-ES in Cup — hmm Cup has \"Vitória da Conquista - BA\" (different base) and... does Cup have \"Vitória - ES\"? Not that I saw; only \"Vitória - BA\" and \"Vitória da Conquista - BA\". OK).\n\nnovo \"Athletico-PR\" 2019 → alias → (atletico, PR) ✓ merges with bm \"Atletico-PR\" ✓ same club.\n\nNow the CRITICAL case — novo bare \"Atlético-MG\"? No: novo uses \"Atlético-MG\" WITH state (UF present) ✓. And bm \"Atletico-MG\" ✓.\n\nOK the registry design holds. One more concern about `finalize`: `dominant = max(stateful, ...)` — for base \"atletico\", stateful = {MG, PR, GO, AC, ES, BA?...} — dominant = MG (most matches). Stateless (atletico, None) — none exists probably. Fine.\n\nNow dataset.py. Key structures:\n\n```python\nclass Dataset:\n    registry: ClubRegistry\n    matches: list[Match]          # canonical (authoritative per comp/season)\n    raw_matches: list[Match]      # all parsed rows from all 5 files\n    players: list[Player]\n    fifa_clubs: dict[str, Club]   # FIFA club string -> club\n    sources: dict[str, dict]      # per-file stats\n    \ndef load_dataset(data_dir: Path | None = None) -> Dataset  (cached)\n```\n\nLoading steps:\n1. Load 5 match CSVs into raw Match objects (fields per file).\n2. Register all team names in registry (raw match rows first, then FIFA clubs).\n3. Count match records per club (add_match_count for home+away teams of every raw row).\n4. Register FIFA clubs (register(club_string)) — their match_count stays 0; player_count incremented per player.\n5. finalize().\n6. Canonical index: group raw by (competition, season) → pick authoritative source by priority → matches list; within chosen source, also dedup (date, home_team, away_team) (safety).\n7. Attach extended stats: BR-Football rows → key (date, home_club.id, away_club.id) → stats; apply to canonical matches with same key (only for matches whose source != BR-Football; brf matches already carry stats).\n\nAuthoritative priority per (competition, season):\n```\nSOURCE_PRIORITY = {\n  'Brasileirao_Matches': 0,\n  'Brazilian_Cup_Matches': 0,\n  'Libertadores_Matches': 0,\n  'novo_campeonato_brasileiro': 1,\n  'BR-Football-Dataset': 2,\n}\n```\nPick min priority among sources present for the group. (bm preferred over novo for 2012-2019 Serie A; Cup file over brf for CdB 2014-2021; brf for 2022-2023 Serie A/B, Serie B/C always, CdB 2022-2023; novo for Serie A 2003-2011.)\n\nWait — one flaw: CdB 2014-2021, Cup file preferred over brf. Cup file 2014: 159 matches; brf 2014 CdB: 43. ✓. What about Libertadores — only lib file. ✓.\n\nCompetition mapping at load:\n- Brasileirao_Matches → \"Brasileirão Serie A\"; round = r['round']; season int.\n- novo → \"Brasileirão Serie A\"; round = Rodada; stadium = Arena; season = Ano.\n- Brazilian_Cup_Matches → \"Copa do Brasil\"; round = r['round']; season.\n- Libertadores_Matches → \"Copa Libertadores\"; stage = r['stage']; season ('NA' → None → the NA row also has no date/score — keep with season None? For search it might show up under \"Flamengo vs Athletico 2022 final\"... but season NA gives no context. I'll keep it with season=None and stage='final'; hmm — actually this row is the 2022 Libertadores final! It'd be nice to attribute season 2022... but from data alone season is 'NA'. The match date is 'NA' too. I'll keep it (goals None, date None, season None) — it appears in Flamengo/Athletico searches and in bracket queries for Libertadores finals listing... with season None it won't show for season=2022. Compromise: keep as-is, honest to source. Actually — hmm, for \"champion(Libertadores, 2022)\" the final rows: stage 'final' + season 'NA' → my champion function filters season==2022 → misses NA row → \"final not in dataset\" — honest answer given no score anyway. OK.\n- BR-Football → tournament mapping: 'Serie A' → Brasileirão Serie A; 'Serie B'; 'Serie C'; 'Copa do Brasil'. Plus stats fields; ht_result/at_result ('WON'/'LOST'/'DRAW' relative to home) — ht_result is home's halftime outcome; ht_diff/at_diff are goal diffs at half? Columns: ht_diff, at_result... spec says \"ht_result, at_result | Half-time results\". Values: WON/LOST/DRAW + floats ht_diff, at_diff. Home ht goals = (home_goals + ht_diff)/2? ht_diff = home_goals_at_HT - away_goals_at_HT presumably. I can reconstruct: ht_home = (total_home_goals + ht_diff)/2? No — ht_diff = home HT goals - away HT goals; final home - final away = ht_diff + at_diff? Let me check with row 1: home 1.0, away 1.0, ht_diff 0.0, at_diff 0.0, ht_result DRAW, at_result DRAW ✓. Row 2: home 0, away 1, ht_diff -1.0, at_diff 1.0, ht_result LOST, at_result WON → HT: 0-1, FT 0-1 → at_diff=+1 means... home scored 0 in 2nd half, away 0? FT 0-1 from HT 0-1: 2nd half 0-0. at_diff 1.0 = second-half diff from home perspective? 0-0 → 0? Hmm at_diff=1? Let me not overinterpret: ht_diff = home-HT − away-HT; at_diff = home-2ndH − away-2ndH? Row2: 2nd half 0-0 → at_diff 0 ≠ 1.0. Alternative: at_diff = away perspective? Let me compute: maybe ht_diff and at_diff are goal DIFFS for home team at HT and FT: ht_diff = HT home-away = -1 ✓; at_diff = FT home-away = -1... but it's 1.0. Hmm at_diff = 1.0 positive. FT diff home−away = −1. |−1|? Or at_diff from away perspective = +1 ✓. Row 1: 0/0 ✓ both DRAW. Let me just store ht_result/at_result labels and ht_diff/at_diff raw as floats, and NOT reconstruct HT goals. Safer. Actually let me do a quick check of a distinctive row to decode... meh. I'll expose kickoff time, corners, shots, attacks + ht/at result labels + diffs. Good enough for the \"Extended Match Statistics\" requirement.\n\nSeason parsing: int or None ('NA').\n\nFIFA loading: relevant columns; skills subset: Crossing, Finishing, HeadingAccuracy, ShortPassing, Volleys, Dribbling, Curve, FKAccuracy, LongPassing, BallControl, Acceleration, SprintSpeed, Agility, Reactions, Balance, ShotPower, Jumping, Stamina, Strength, LongShots, Aggression, Interceptions, Positioning, Vision, Penalties, Composure, StandingTackle, SlidingTackle. Parse ints where possible.\n\nFIFA club → registry: register(club string) → TeamName; club = registry.get(...) AFTER finalize. So sequence: register match teams, count matches, THEN register FIFA clubs (variant counts only), THEN finalize? No wait — finalize merges stateless into stateful. FIFA \"Santos\" (santos, None) must merge into (santos, SP). If I register FIFA clubs BEFORE finalize, the (santos, None) club gets created with 0 matches; if novo already created (santos, None) with 500 matches — same club key, counters add ✓. Then finalize merges into (santos, SP) ✓. Player counts: assign AFTER finalize via registry.get(normalize(club_string)).\n\nBut WAIT — foreign FIFA clubs like \"Alanyaspor\" → (alanyaspor, None) — no stateful same-base club → survives as own club ✓ with player_count. And \"Atlético Madrid\" → (atleticomadrid, None) → survives ✓.\n\nEdge: FIFA \"Vitória\" (vitoria, None) merges into (vitoria, BA) — and FIFA \"Vitória Guimarães\" → (vitoriaguimaraes, None) → no same-base stateful → own club ✓. \"Vitória de Setúbal\" → (vitoriadesetubal, None) ✓ own.\n\nEdge: FIFA \"Santos Laguna\" → (santosl, ...) wait — \"Santos Laguna\" tokens [santos, laguna] → base \"santoslaguna\" ✓ own club (Mexican). Does it merge? Base \"santoslaguna\" ≠ \"santos\" ✓ no merge. But resolve(\"Santos\") → Tier 1 (santos, None)→merged→(santos,SP) ✓ only SP. resolve(\"Santos Laguna\") → Tier 1 exact (santoslaguna, None) club ✓.\n\nEdge: FIFA \"Internacional\" → (internacional, None) → merges into (internacional, RS) ✓ (RS has more records than SC). ✓\n\nNow — \"player_count\" for clubs: count players whose club string resolves to that club id. Also FIFA club strings map kept for player search by club: find_player(club='Grêmio') → match player.club strings by normalized containment OR via registry club resolution: resolve club query → club → players whose _club_team maps to same club id. The registry path handles \"Sport Recife\" ↔ \"Sport Club do Recife\" automatically ✓. But foreign clubs (\"Chelsea\") → resolve → (chelsea, None) club ✓ players attach. Player search by club: resolve query → best club → filter players by club id. Plus fallback: substring on raw club strings. I'll do: resolve via registry; if no resolution, substring on raw strings.\n\nExtended stats join: build dict from brf rows: key (date, home_club_id, away_club_id) — careful: use club ids post-finalize. For canonical matches from other sources: same key → attach stats. But note: brf might have multiple rows same key (2021 dupes) — keep first with stats.\n\nAlso there's a subtle issue: canonical CdB 2014-2021 from Cup file; brf CdB stats join via (date, clubs) — do Cup file dates align with brf dates? Maybe often. Best-effort ✓.\n\nMatch display names: use raw source names (home_name/away_name) — for canonical bm matches: \"Flamengo-RJ\" etc. Hmm — spec examples display \"Flamengo\". For nicer output, canonical Match.to_dict could use club.display? But home_name preserves source fidelity. I'll display club.display in to_dict via club lookup? Match doesn't hold club refs... I have _home_club/_away_club fields (ids). to_dict uses home_name. Let me instead set home_name to the CLUB DISPLAY at build time for canonical matches? But then \"source\" raw fidelity lost — acceptable? The spec example output: \"2023-09-03: Flamengo 2-1 Fluminense (Brasileirão Round 22)\" — display names without state. I'll make canonical matches carry display names via club registry, while raw_matches keep source spellings. Hmm, but Cup matches include obscure teams (\"4 de Julho - PI\") — club.display falls back to most-common variant ✓ fine.\n\nWait, but then within canonical matches, \"Flamengo-RJ\" (bm) and \"Flamengo\" (brf 2022) both display \"Flamengo\" ✓ consistent — GOOD for dedup display.\n\nDecision: for canonical matches: home_name = club_display(home club) + (f\" ({state})\"? no — plain display). Raw matches keep original spellings.\n\nHmm — but Vasco display \"Vasco da Gama\" vs novo raw \"Vasco\" — canonical shows \"Vasco da Gama\" consistently ✓.\n\nOne risk: display for obscure clubs = most-common variant which might be ugly (\"Boavista Sport Club (antigo Esporte Clube Barreira) - RJ\"). Fine.\n\nCup \"round\" display: keep numeric string. Bracket tool labels final.\n\nNow write dataset.py.\n\nAlso, Dataset needs per-(competition, season) source info for competition_info: dict[(comp, season)] → source used + counts.\n\nAnd skipped-rows stats: rows skipped (no date AND no teams?), count.\n\nLet me write it.","format":"unknown","index":0}]}},"id":"prt_05d37cacf001HPX0yP0txNrRgl","sessionID":"ses_fa2db0ef4ffeemTLK4uNaaAd5c","messageID":"msg_05d359a950016r5eH58CObl1VE"}}
