t now! Look at the earlier exploration output again — it says:\n```\nBrasileirao matches: 4180\nseasons: ['2012', '2013', '2014', '2015', '2016', '2017', '2018', '2019', '2020', '2021']\n```\nHmm wait, maybe it didn't. Let me scroll back... The message says:\n\"Brasileirao matches: 4180\nseasons: ['2012', '2013', '2014', '2015', '2016', '2017', '2018', '2019', '2020', '2021']\"\n\nHmm, no — actually it says \"seasons: ['2012', '2013', '2014', '2015', '2016', '2017', '2018', '2019', '2020', '2021']\"... I can't resolve this discrepancy by memory-guessing. It doesn't matter: the current direct Counter is authoritative: 2012-2022, 4180 total, 380 each. My implementation reads the same file and shows 2022 ✓. Moving on.\n\nActually — hmm, one thing: that earlier script might have had `max_episodes`-like nothing... let me just drop it. The important thing: current pipeline is correct.\n\nWait, actually I realize I should double check one thing — the very first exploration printed exactly:\n\n\"Brasileirao matches: 4180\nseasons: ['2012', '2013', '2014', '2015', '2016', '2017', '2018', '2019', '2020', '2021']\"\n\nvs now Counter({'2012': 380, ..., '2022': 380}) = 11 seasons × 380 = 4180. The earlier print listed 10 seasons for 4180 matches — internally inconsistent, so the earlier output must have been misprinted/truncated somehow. Fine. Truth: 2012-2022.\n\nNow — canonical counts:\n- 2003-2011: novo (9 seasons)\n- 2012-2022: bm (11 seasons)\n- 2023: brf (377)\n\nAlso interesting: bm 2022 last round has NA goals — my parse handles it (has_score False) ✓. Standings 2022 will count 379 scored matches; Coritiba/Palmeiras... official 2022 champion = Palmeiras (81 pts). Let me verify standings for 2022 and 2023 quickly, plus check CdB/Libertadores groupings. Then write service.py.\n\nLet me also check the 2023 brf season: 377 matches — nearly complete; standings 2023 official champion: Palmeiras 82? (2023: Palmeiras 82? Actually 2023 champion Palmeiras with 82 pts? 2023 Série A