{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1788270534611,"sessionID":"ses_fa2db0ef4ffeemTLK4uNaaAd5c","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"bash","callID":"call_bb3c18293bf0438b960f22ef","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"command":"venv/bin/python - <<'EOF'\nfrom brazilian_soccer_mcp.dataset import load_dataset\nds = load_dataset()\n\n# scored matches per (comp, season) for Serie A\nfrom collections import defaultdict\ntot = defaultdict(int); scored = defaultdict(int)\nfor m in ds.matches:\n    if m.competition == 'Brasileirão Serie A':\n        tot[m.season] += 1\n        if m.has_score: scored[m.season] += 1\nfor s in sorted(tot):\n    if s and s >= 2020: print(s, \"total:\", tot[s], \"scored:\", scored[s])\n\ndef standings2(comp, season):\n    st = {}\n    for m in ds.matches:\n        if m.competition != comp or m.season != season or not m.has_score: continue\n        st.setdefault(m._home_club, [0]*9); st.setdefault(m._away_club, [0]*9)\n        h, a = st[m._home_club], st[m._away_club]\n        hg, ag = m.home_goals, m.away_goals\n        h[0]+=1; a[0]+=1\n        h[4]+=hg; h[5]+=ag; a[4]+=ag; a[5]+=hg\n        if hg>ag: h[1]+=1; a[3]+=1; h[8]+=3\n        elif hg<ag: a[1]+=1; h[3]+=1; a[8]+=3\n        else: h[2]+=1; a[2]+=1; h[8]+=1; a[8]+=1\n    return sorted(st.items(), key=lambda kv: (-kv[1][8], -(kv[1][4]-kv[1][5]), -kv[1][4]))\n\nfor season in (2022, 2023):\n    print(f\"== Serie A {season} ==\")\n    for cid, v in standings2('Brasileirão Serie A', season)[:4]:\n        print(f\"   {cid:22} P{v[0]} W{v[1]} D{v[2]} L{v[3]} GF{v[4]} GA{v[5]} Pts{v[8]}\")\nEOF"},"output":"2020 total: 380 scored: 380\n2021 total: 380 scored: 380\n2022 total: 380 scored: 299\n2023 total: 377 scored: 377\n== Serie A 2022 ==\n   palmeiras|SP           P30 W19 D9 L2 GF52 GA20 Pts66\n   internacional|RS       P30 W14 D12 L4 GF44 GA26 Pts54\n   fluminense|RJ          P30 W15 D6 L9 GF48 GA36 Pts51\n   corinthians|SP         P30 W14 D9 L7 GF36 GA29 Pts51\n== Serie A 2023 ==\n   gremio|RS              P38 W21 D5 L12 GF63 GA55 Pts68\n   palmeiras|SP           P37 W19 D10 L8 GF61 GA32 Pts67\n   atletico|MG            P38 W19 D9 L10 GF52 GA32 Pts66\n   flamengo|RJ            P38 W19 D9 L10 GF56 GA42 Pts66\n","metadata":{"output":"2020 total: 380 scored: 380\n2021 total: 380 scored: 380\n2022 total: 380 scored: 299\n2023 total: 377 scored: 377\n== Serie A 2022 ==\n   palmeiras|SP           P30 W19 D9 L2 GF52 GA20 Pts66\n   internacional|RS       P30 W14 D12 L4 GF44 GA26 Pts54\n   fluminense|RJ          P30 W15 D6 L9 GF48 GA36 Pts51\n   corinthians|SP         P30 W14 D9 L7 GF36 GA29 Pts51\n== Serie A 2023 ==\n   gremio|RS              P38 W21 D5 L12 GF63 GA55 Pts68\n   palmeiras|SP           P37 W19 D10 L8 GF61 GA32 Pts67\n   atletico|MG            P38 W19 D9 L10 GF52 GA32 Pts66\n   flamengo|RJ            P38 W19 D9 L10 GF56 GA42 Pts66\n","exit":0,"truncated":false},"title":"venv/bin/python - <<'EOF'\nfrom brazilian_soccer_mcp.dataset import load_dataset\nds = load_dataset()\n\n# scored matches per (comp, season) for Serie A\nfrom collections import defaultdict\ntot = defaultdict(int); scored = defaultdict(int)\nfor m in ds.matches:\n    if m.competition == 'Brasileirão Serie A':\n        tot[m.season] += 1\n        if m.has_score: scored[m.season] += 1\nfor s in sorted(tot):\n    if s and s >= 2020: print(s, \"total:\", tot[s], \"scored:\", scored[s])\n\ndef standings2(comp, season):\n    st = {}\n    for m in ds.matches:\n        if m.competition != comp or m.season != season or not m.has_score: continue\n        st.setdefault(m._home_club, [0]*9); st.setdefault(m._away_club, [0]*9)\n        h, a = st[m._home_club], st[m._away_club]\n        hg, ag = m.home_goals, m.away_goals\n        h[0]+=1; a[0]+=1\n        h[4]+=hg; h[5]+=ag; a[4]+=ag; a[5]+=hg\n        if hg>ag: h[1]+=1; a[3]+=1; h[8]+=3\n        elif hg<ag: a[1]+=1; h[3]+=1; a[8]+=3\n        else: h[2]+=1; a[2]+=1; h[8]+=1; a[8]+=1\n    return sorted(st.items(), key=lambda kv: (-kv[1][8], -(kv[1][4]-kv[1][5]), -kv[1][4]))\n\nfor season in (2022, 2023):\n    print(f\"== Serie A {season} ==\")\n    for cid, v in standings2('Brasileirão Serie A', season)[:4]:\n        print(f\"   {cid:22} P{v[0]} W{v[1]} D{v[2]} L{v[3]} GF{v[4]} GA{v[5]} Pts{v[8]}\")\nEOF","time":{"start":1788270534563,"end":1788270534608}},"metadata":{"openrouter":{"reasoning_details":[{"type":"reasoning.text","text":"There's a BUG in my scratch standings code (not the library): the draw branch never increments draws — look: W19 D11 L0 for palmeiras with P30 — draws counted in D? \"W19 D11 L0\" → 19+11+0=30 ✓ hmm D=11... wait I printed v[2] as D and never incremented v[1] on draws... let me look: draw branch does `h[2]+=1; a[2]+=1` — v[2] IS draws. W = v[1]. So D11 for Palmeiras with L = 30-19-11 = 0 losses?? Palmeiras 2022 lost 5 games! P30 W19 D11 L0 — 2022 Palmeiras played 38! P30 means only 30 matches counted — because bm 2022 has NA scores in later rounds?? Earlier I found only ONE NA row (the last). But P30 for everyone...\n\nOH WAIT. I see — the 2022 canonical matches: 380 rows, but maybe many late-season rows have NA scores (dataset captured mid-season?). Let me check: how many 2022 matches have scores? And the draw-count bug: L = P-W-D → L0 for ALL teams is impossible. Let me recheck my scratch code... \n\n`if m.home_goals > m.away_goals: h[1]+=1; a[2]+=1; h[6]+=3` — home win: home W+1 ✓, away L... a[2]+=1 — I used v[2] for LOSSES?? And draws also increment h[2]! So v[2] mixes losses AND draws. My scratch code is buggy — losses and draws both went to v[2]. So \"D11\" is actually draws+losses combined. Fine — scratch bug, not library bug. Palmeiras P30: hmm still odd.\n\nLet me redo the scratch properly AND check 2022 scored-match count. Also 2023: Grêmio P38 W21 D17?? draws+losses mixed again. Official 2023: Palmeiras champion 82 pts, Grêmio 79... here Grêmio 68?? and P37/38 with brf 2023 (377 matches). Something's off — 2023 official: Palmeiras 82, Grêmio 79, Atlético 74?... Actually no: 2023 Série A final: 1. Palmeiras 82; 2. Grêmio 79? Hmm, I recall Palmeiras 82, Botafogo... let me not trust memory; but the computed table has Grêmio first with 68 — suspicious.\n\nWAIT. P38 W21 D17 L0 → wins 21 × 3 = 63 + draws... if D17 → 63+17 = 80 ≠ 68. So D=17 includes losses: W21, (D+L)=17, Pts 68 = 63+5 → D5 L12?? A team with 12 losses winning the league? Impossible. My scratch math is just wrong somewhere. Let me rewrite the scratch standings carefully and also count scored matches per season.","format":"unknown","index":0}]}},"id":"prt_05d3adc05001PlR1HsZd0WLzUV","sessionID":"ses_fa2db0ef4ffeemTLK4uNaaAd5c","messageID":"msg_05d3a6b56001dXmzJyhGeGn1KB"}}
