real problems are where THE SAME club has different bases across sources. Critical ones (affecting Serie A/B/C canonical data, since brf is authoritative for 2023 Serie A and all Serie B/C):\n\nFrom the audit + the earlier 2023 team table:\n1. `fortalezafc` (brf 2023) vs `fortaleza` (bm \"Fortaleza-CE\"). bm raw name is \"Fortaleza-CE\" → base \"fortaleza\" + state CE → key \"fortaleza|CE\". Wait — earlier audit shows 'fortaleza' (BR-Football) <-> 'fortalezaec' and 'fortalezafc' — hold on, where does base \"fortalezaec\" come from? bm has \"Fortaleza-CE\" → base \"fortaleza\". \"fortalezaec\"... Cup file probably has \"Fortaleza EC - CE\"? And brf has BOTH \"Fortaleza\" and \"Fortaleza FC\" spellings?! The audit shows brf contains 'fortaleza', 'fortalezafc'; and Cup contains 'fortalezaec'. Let me get precise: which sources contain which Fortaleza spellings. Since all have state CE (or none), the KEYS differ only by base: fortaleza|CE, fortalezafc|, fortalezaec|CE... The stateless \"fortalezafc|\" won't merge (no same-base stateful). ALIAS FIX: \"fortalezafc\" → (\"fortaleza\", \"CE\"); \"fortalezaec\" → (\"fortaleza\", \"CE\").\n\n2. `bragantino` (brf) vs `redbullbragantino` (bm). ALIAS: \"bragantino\" → (\"redbullbragantino\", \"SP\").\n\n3. `ecinternacional` (brf) vs `internacional` (bm/Cup/Lib/fifa). Hmm — \"ecinternacional\"... wait, brf has \"EC Internacional\"?? Hmm — actually looking at audit: 'ecinternacional' (BR-Football) — but ALSO 'internacional' (BR-Football). Both? Serie B has \"Inter de Lages\"? Hmm, \"EC Internacional\" hmm. Wait — is \"EC Internacional\" maybe a DIFFERENT club? Hmm. Let me check raw names. Actually hold on — I don't think I need to resolve every small club. The critical canonical competitions: Serie A/B/C (brf authoritative for B/C and 2023 A) + bm/cup/lib files (dedicated, internally consistent). Split identities only matter when the SAME competition-season mixes sources (never — one source per season) OR when a user queries across