rana\", \"PR\")\n9. `santacruzfc` → (\"santacruz\", \"PE\") — \"Santa Cruz RN\"/\"RS\" keep states ✓\n10. `fcatleticocearense` → (\"atleticocearense\", \"CE\")\n11. `clubedoremo` → (\"remo\", \"PA\")\n12. `gremionovorizontino` → (\"novorizontino\", \"SP\")? Hmm — wait: is Cup \"Novorizontino - SP\" really Grêmio Novorizontino? Let me think — no wait, there's a subtlety: Grêmio Novorizontino... The club \"Grêmio Novorizontino\" from Novo Horizonte-SP plays Série B 2020s. Cup \"Novorizontino - SP\" — same club, the Kaggle authors shortened. Alias ✓.\n13. `ecinternacional` → (\"internacional\", \"SC\") — the SC club. Wait, actually brf \"EC Internacional SC\" — hmm, but could also be \"EC Internacional\" of... state SC given. Cup \"Internacional - SC\" ✓ same. Alias with state SC.\n14. `sercaxias` → (\"caxias\", \"RS\") — \"Ser Caxias - RS\" = SER Caxias (Sociedade Esportiva e Recreativa Caxias do Sul) = same as \"Caxias - RS\" ✓ alias.\n15. `operariofc` → (\"operario\", \"MS\") — \"Operario FC MS\" = Operário-MS (Campo Grande)? Hmm — Operário Ferroviário is PR (Ponta Grossa); Operário-MS (Campo Grande) is a different club that played Série B 2020s! \"Operario FC MS\" state MS → alias → (\"operario\", \"MS\") ✓ matches Cup \"Operário - MS\" ✓.\n16. `operarioferroviarioesportec` → (\"operario\", \"PR\").\n17. `brasildepelotas` — brf \"Brasil de Pelotas\" stateless; Cup \"Brasil - RS\" → (brasil, RS)!! So Cup spells it \"Brasil - RS\" (base brasil, state RS) and brf spells \"Brasil de Pelotas\" (base brasildepelotas). SPLIT both ways! Fix: alias \"brasildepelotas\" → (\"brasil\", \"RS\")... but also Cup has \"Brasília FC\"? \"brasiliafc\" distinct ✓. And \"brasil\" (brf stateless)? Not present in brf per dump (only cup has 'brasil' with RS). OK: alias \"brasildepelotas\" → (\"brasil\", \"RS\").\n18. `saojosepoa` (\"Sao Jose - POA\", brf stateless) → (\"saojose\", \"RS\") — São José-RS (POA = Porto Alegre) ✓.\n19. `riverplate` — Cup \"River Plate - SE\" (state SE, Brazilian River Plate-SE) vs Libertadores \"River Plate\" (stateless, Argentine) vs FIFA \"River Plate\"?? — hmm FIFA club \"River Plate\" (Argentine) → (riverplate, None) → merges into... (riverplate, SE)?! That would attach the Argentine River Plate players to the Sergipe club! BAD. Check: is there a stateful riverplate? Cup \"River Plate - SE\" → yes (riverplate, SE). FIFA \"River Plate\" (Argentine) → (riverplate, None) → merge into (riverplate, SE) — WRONG.\n    Fix: alias \"riverplate\" stateless → hmm. I need a way to distinguish. FIFA \"River Plate\" is Argentine; Lib \"River Plate\" is Argentine. Cup \"River Plate - SE\" is Brazilian. The stateless one should NOT merge into SE. But my merge rule does it automatically. \n    Options: (a) alias \"riverplate\" → (\"riverplate\", None)?? — no-op, merge still happens. (b) Add merge-blocklist: bases where stateless variants should NOT merge: {\"riverplate\", \"nacional\", ...}. Hmm — nacional: Lib \"Nacional (URU)\" → base \"nacionaluru\" ✓ distinct already (parens kept). Lib \"Nacional (PAR)\" → \"nacionalpar\" ✓. FIFA \"CD Nacional\" → \"cdnacional\" ✓. So nacional is fine.\n    For riverplate: stateless (riverplate, None) has Lib matches (Argentine finals!) + FIFA players (Argentine). (riverplate, SE) has Cup matches. Merge attaches ~30 Lib matches to the SE club — bad for queries \"River Plate\". FIX: add a small \"NO_MERGE_BASES\" set containing \"riverplate\" (and maybe others as discovered). Actually — better: make the merge only apply when the stateless club's variants suggest Brazil... too clever. Simple blocklist: {\"riverplate\"}. Any others? Let me think of foreign clubs with Brazilian state-qualified same-base twins: \"Barcelona\" — Lib \"Barcelona-EQU\" → base \"barcelonaequ\" ✓ distinct. \"Arsenal\" → \"arsenalsarandi\" ✓. \"Botafogo\" — FIFA \"Botafogo\" (Brazilian RJ) ✓ correct merge. \"Sport\" — FIFA \"Sport Club do Recife\" → alias ✓; \"Sporting Cristal\" distinct base ✓. \"Inter\" (fifa \"Inter\" = Internazionale!) vs Cup \"Inter - ?\"... hmm! FIFA club \"Inter\" (Milan) → (inter, None) → merges into stateful (inter, XX) if exists — Cup has \"Interporto\"? no that's interporto. Does Cup have \"Inter - RJ\" or \"Inter - SP\"?? Hmm — brf has \"Inter\" stateless (audit: 'inter' (BR-Football)...). brf \"Inter\" stateless = Inter de Limeira? (Serie C) or Inter-RS? Let me check raw... The audit showed 'inter' in brf, cup, lib, fifa. If brf \"Inter\" stateless = Inter de Limeira SP, and it merges into (inter, RS)?? Is there a stateful (inter, RS)? \"Internacional-RS\" is base \"internacional\" not \"inter\". So (inter, None) has no stateful same-base → stays own club. Then FIFA \"Inter\" (Milan) players + brf \"Inter\" matches share club (inter, None) — mildly wrong but harmless for a demo (Brazilian focus). Skip.\n    So blocklist: just \"riverplate\". Hmm — also \"nacional\"? Lib bare \"Nacional\"? No — all Lib nacionals have parens. Cup \"Nacional - ?\"... audit showed 'nacional' (Brazilian_Cup_Matches)! Cup has \"Nacional - AM\" or similar → stateful (nacional, XX). FIFA \"CD Nacional\" → cdnacional distinct ✓. Lib \"Nacional (URU)\" → nacionaluru ✓. So no bare (nacional, None) except... brf? audit: 'nacional' (BR-Football-Dataset) ↔ ... brf has \"Nacional\" stateless (Serie C: Nacional-AM). Merges into stateful (nacional, AM) from Cup? ✓ correct (same club!). Fine.\n    \n    So NO_MERGE = {\"riverplate\"}. Also double-check \"atleticomadrid\"? No stateful twin ✓. \"botafogo\" — FIFA Botafogo merges to RJ ✓ desired. \n\n20. `guarany` vs `guarani` — Cup \"Guarany - CE\" vs \"Guarani - CE\": different spellings, probably same club (Guarany de Juazeiro-CE)? Or Guarani-SP vs Guarany-CE are different. \"guarany|CE\" vs \"guarani|CE\" — different bases, same state. Hmm — Guarany (with Y) CE — brf also has \"Guarany de Sobral\"?? audit: 'guarany' (brf) <-> 'guaranydesobral' (cup). So \"Guarany - CE\" = Guarany de Sobral probably. And \"Guarani - CE\" = Guarani de Juazeiro. DIFFERENT clubs ✓ keep separate. OK.\n\n21. `icasa` → stateless brf merges into Cup (icasa, CE) ✓ automatic.\n\n22. `asa` → brf \"ASA\" stateless merges into (asa, AL) ✓ automatic. Note brf \"ASA AL\" state AL ✓ same club.\n\n23. `abc` → brf \"ABC\" stateless merges into (abc, RN) ✓.\n\n24. `crb` → stateless merges into (crb, AL) ✓. \n\n25. `csa` \"C.s.a. - AL\" → tokens \"c\",\"s\",\"a\",\"AL\" → base \"csa\" ✓ (join no spaces) — nice.\n\n26. `uniao` Cup \"União - MT\" stateful (uniao, MT); brf \"Uniao Rondonopolis\"? → base \"uniaorondonopolis\" — alias → (\"uniao\", \"MT\")? União Rondonópolis-MT vs \"União - MT\"... hmm, \"União - MT\" might BE União Rondonópolis. Skip (minor).\n\nOK also — \"Internacional\" in Libertadores stateless merges to (internacional, RS) ✓ correct (Inter-RS played Lib).\n\nOne more important check — **Libertadores foreign teams that are stateless and could wrongly merge**: \"Boca Juniors\" (bocajuniors, None) — no stateful twin ✓. \"Palmeiras\" Lib stateless → (palmeiras, SP) ✓. \"Corinthians\" ✓. \"Grêmio\" ✓. \"São Paulo\" ✓. \"Santos\" ✓ (SP). \"Vasco\" ✓ RJ. \"Cruzeiro\" ✓ MG. \"Fluminense\" ✓ RJ. \"Botafogo\" ✓ RJ. \"Flamengo\" ✓ RJ. \"Athletico\" → alias PR ✓. \"Atlético-MG\" ✓ MG. All correct!\n\nNow, also check \"Ceara\" brf stateless → merges (ceara, CE) ✓. \"Cuiaba\" stateless → (cuiaba, MT) ✓ (also \"Cuiaba MT\" stateful same). \"Bahia\" → ecbahia alias + stateless merge ✓.\n\nLet me now write the final alias additions into normalize.py. Also the NO_MERGE set needs support in registry.finalize(). I'll add `NO_MERGE_BASES = {\"riverplate\"}` in normalize.py and import in registry.\n\nFinal aliases to ADD (beyond existing):\n```\n\"fortalezafc\": (\"fortaleza\", \"CE\"),\n\"fortalezaec\": (\"fortaleza\", \"CE\"),\n\"bragantino\": (\"redbullbragantino\", \"SP\"),\n\"ecjuventude\": (\"juventude\", \"RS\"),\n\"ecvitoria\": (\"vitoria\", \"BA\"),\n\"vitoriaec\": (\"vitoria\", \"BA\"),\n\"csalagoano\": (\"csa\", \"AL\"),\n\"nauticocapibaribe\": (\"nautico\", \"PE\"),\n\"portuguesadesportos\": (\"portuguesa\", \"SP\"),\n\"caparana\": (\"parana\", \"PR\"),\n\"santacruzfc\": (\"santacruz\", \"PE\"),\n\"fcatleticocearense\": (\"atleticocearense\", \"CE\"),\n\"clubedoremo\": (\"remo\", \"PA\"),\n\"gremionovorizontino\": (\"novorizontino\", \"SP\"),\n\"ecinternacional\": (\"internacional\", \"SC\"),\n\"sercaxias\": (\"caxias\", \"RS\"),\n\"operariofc\": (\"operario\", \"MS\"),\n\"operarioferroviarioesportec\": (\"operario\", \"PR\"),\n\"brasildepelotas\": (\"brasil\", \"RS\"),\n\"saojosepoa\": (\"saojose\", \"RS\"),\n```\n\nWait — careful with \"novorizontino\": Cup \"Novorizontino - SP\" → (novorizontino, SP) exists as stateful club. brf \"Gremio Novorizontino\" stateless → alias → (\"novorizontino\", \"SP\") ✓.\n\nAnd \"saojosepoa\" → (\"saojose\", \"RS\"): Cup \"São José - RS\" stateful (saojose, RS) ✓; brf \"São José - POA\" stateless → alias ✓. But brf also has \"Sao Jose PA\" (state PA — different club) ✓ preserved, and \"Sao Jose RS\" (stateful ✓).\n\n\"brasildepelotas\" → (\"brasil\", \"RS\"): Cup \"Brasil - RS\" stateful (brasil, RS) ✓.\n\nHmm — \"caxias\" — brf \"Caxias\" stateless + \"Caxias RS\" stateful; Cup \"Caxias - RS\" ✓ → all (caxias, RS) via merge ✓ automatic. \"sercaxias\" alias ✓.\n\n\"oeste\": brf \"Oeste\" stateless → merges into Cup (oeste, SP) ✓ automatic.\n\n\"remo\": brf \"Remo\" stateless → merges (remo, PA) ✓; \"Remo PA\" stateful ✓; \"Clube Do Remo\" alias ✓.\n\n\"realnoroeste\": brf \"Real Noroeste\" stateless → merges into (realnoroeste, ES)? Cup \"Real Noroeste - ES\" stateful ✓ automatic ✓.\n\nAlso \"guarani\": brf \"Guarani SP\"/\"Guarani-SP\" stateful (guarani, SP); Cup \"Guarani - SP\" ✓; novo \"Guarani\" stateless → merges (guarani, SP) ✓ (correct — the famous Guarani-SP played 2003-2004). ✓ \n\nOne more — \"nautico\": novo \"Náutico\" stateless merges into... stateful nautico: (nautico, PE) [bm/Cup] and (nautico, RR) [brf \"Nautico RR\", Cup \"Nautico - RR\"]. Merge → most records = PE ✓ correct.\n\n\"juventude\": novo stateless → (juventude, RS) most records ✓; brf \"Juventude MA\" distinct ✓.\n\n\"vitoria\": novo \"Vitória\" stateless → stateful: (vitoria, BA) + (vitoria, ES) [brf \"Vitoria ES\"] → merges into BA (more records) ✓ correct (novo's Vitória = BA).\n\n\"santacruz\": novo stateless → stateful: (santacruz, PE), (santacruz, RN), (santacruz, RS) → PE (most records) ✓ correct.\n\n\"ceara\": novo stateless → (ceara, CE) ✓. \"bahia\" → BA ✓. \"parana\": novo/fifa/brf stateless → (parana, PR) ✓.\n\nAlso fifa \"Paraná\" → (parana, None) → merge (parana, PR) ✓.\n\nAlright — also NO_MERGE_BASES = {\"riverplate\"} in registry.finalize: skip merging for stateless clubs whose base is in the set. Then (riverplate, None) stays separate: Lib Argentine River Plate + FIFA River Plate players there; Cup River Plate-SE separate ✓. But queries \"River Plate\" → tier 2: two clubs (riverplate| None and |SE) ranked by records — None has more (Lib finals) ✓ good.\n\nLet me apply these changes now.","format":"unknown","index":0}]}},"id":"prt_05d3f4988001hYWKMzljkQ5KOV","sessionID":"ses_fa2db0ef4ffeemTLK4uNaaAd5c","messageID":"msg_05d3e2c4b001lnH8E8U1iu52AW"}}
