 D, \"home goals:\", hg, \"away goals:\", ag)\n    # goals sanity: any goals > 10?\n    weird = [m for m in ms if (m.home_goals or 0) > 9 or (m.away_goals or 0) > 9]\n    for m in weird[:5]: print(\"   weird:\", m.date, m.home_name, m.score, m.away_name)\nEOF","time":{"start":1788271344457,"end":1788271344504}},"metadata":{"openrouter":{"reasoning_details":[{"type":"reasoning.text","text":"Interesting!! The 2023 table now shows:\n- 16. Santos 43 pts — EXACTLY their official 2023 total (43 pts, 17th... wait Santos finished 17th officially? hmm — official 2023: 16. Bahia 44? 17. Santos 43? relegated: 17º Santos 43, 18º Goiás 39? hmm, actually official relegated: Coritiba (19th? 30 pts?), Goiás, América-MG... and SANTOS. That's 4: Santos, Goiás, Coritiba, América? No wait — 17th Santos also relegated (bottom 4 = 17-20). Official: 17 Santos 43, 18 Goiás 39, 19 Coritiba 30?, 20 América 24? — hmm let me check: official 2023 relegation zone: Santos (17th, 43), Goiás (18th, 39?), Coritiba (19th, 30?), América-MG (20th, 24?). Vasco SURVIVED with 42 pts?? NO WAIT — Vasco finished 2023 with... hmm, Vasco had 42 pts and stayed up?! Actually YES — I now remember: Vasco survived (15th? 16th?), Santos relegated with MORE points than Vasco?? No no — Vasco 2023: 42 points, finished 15th? That doesn't work — 42 < 43.\n\nHmm, hold on. Let me look at my computed table: Santos 43 (16th), Vasco 42 (17th), Goiás 39, Coritiba 30, América 24. The computed relegated (bottom 4) = Vasco, Goiás, Coritiba, América. But REALITY: Santos was relegated; Vasco survived. Santos 43 > Vasco 42 means in the computed table Santos is ABOVE Vasco.\n\nBUT actually — wait. What was Vasco's real 2023 total? Let me think... 2023 final: 1 Palmeiras 82, 2 Grêmio 79? — my computed Grêmio is 68, which would be 2nd here. Real Grêmio 2023: hmm. Let me reconsider — maybe the real table WAS: 1. Palmeiras 82, 2. Grêmio 79, 3. Atlético 74, 4. Flamengo 71, 5. Botafogo 64? — Botafogo 64 is CONFIRMED by data. If real top-5 