 -153,8 +153,9 @@\n height: Optional[str]\n weight: Optional[str]\n skills: dict[str, int] = field(default_factory=dict)\n _club_team: Optional[TeamName] = field(default=None, repr=False)\n+_club_id: Optional[str] = field(default=None, repr=False)  # merged club id\n \n def to_dict(self) -> dict:\n     return {\n         \"id\": self.player_id,\n","additions":1,"deletions":0},"truncated":false},"title":"brazilian_soccer_mcp/models.py","time":{"start":1788271504997,"end":1788271504998}},"metadata":{"openrouter":{"reasoning_details":[{"type":"reasoning.text","text":"Also `_club_team_from_key` is defined AFTER `derby_matches` uses it — Python resolves at call time so it works, but cleaner to move it up. Actually it's fine (function called at runtime after module load). But there's a subtle bug: `key.rpartition(\"|\")` — for key \"flamengo|RJ\" → base \"flamengo\", state \"RJ\" ✓. For \"riverplate|\" → rpartition gives (\"riverplate\", \"|\", \"\") → state \"\" → None ✓. OK good.\n\nAlso in `players_at_club` and `_player_matches` I compare `p._club_team.key == target.id` — but club ids are like \"flamengo|RJ\" and TeamName.key is \"flamengo|RJ\" (with state) or \"flamengo|\" (without) ✓ consistent formats. BUT WAIT — there's a mismatch: `p._club_team` is the normalized team of the FIFA club STRING — e.g. \"Grêmio\" → TeamName(\"gremio\", None) → key \"gremio|\". The club id for Grêmio after merge is \"gremio|RS\"! So comparing `p._club_team.key == \"gremio|RS\"` FAILS. In `find_players` with club filter and `players_at_club`, I must resolve via `ds.club_id(p._club_team)` (which goes through the registry's merged lookup) rather than comparing raw keys.\n\nBut `ds.club_id()` does registry.get(team) → _by_id lookup → correct post-merge club id ✓. Let me fix: build an index fifa_club_id per player once (during dataset build I already compute player counts via registry.get — but I don't STORE the resolved club id on the player). Let me store it: in build_dataset step 7, set `p._club_team` AND compute a resolved club id. I'll add a field `_club_id` on Player, set during build. Then `_player_matches` compares `p._club_id == club_id`, and `players_at_club` filters `p._club_id == target.id`. And team_profile's player filter uses `p._club_id == club.id`.\n\nLet me update models.Player to add `_club_id: Optional[str]`, dataset build to set it, and service to use it.","format":"unknown","index":0}]}},"id":"prt_05d49ae5f001WMa37d9Cr5btKM","sessionID":"ses_fa2db0ef4ffeemTLK4uNaaAd5c","messageID":"msg_05d497159001BLso7u6pIIPd4z"}}
