{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1788271740217,"sessionID":"ses_fa2db0ef4ffeemTLK4uNaaAd5c","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"write","callID":"call_bde5e5ecaade4530a14dcf28","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"content":"#!/usr/bin/env python\n\"\"\"\nEntry point: Brazilian Soccer MCP server (stdio transport).\n\nContext block\n-------------\nWhy:\n    TASK.md requires an MCP server; MCP clients launch servers as\n    subprocesses with a stdio JSON-RPC transport, so a thin launcher script\n    at the repository root is the most client-friendly entry point.\n\nWhat:\n    Delegates to ``brazilian_soccer_mcp.server:main`` (FastMCP stdio).\n    Configure any MCP client with:\n        {\"command\": \"python\", \"args\": [\"<repo>/server.py\"]}\n    or install the package and use the ``brazilian-soccer-mcp`` console\n    script.\n\nTest:\n    Covered by the stdio round-trip scenario in ``tests/test_server.py``.\n\nSpec references:\n    TASK.md \"Overview\" and \"References\" -> MCP Protocol\n    (https://modelcontextprotocol.io).\n\"\"\"\n\nfrom brazilian_soccer_mcp.server import main\n\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    main()\n","filePath":"/Users/maui/.retort/work/retort-local-8zur77lj/retort-2e29d1db74f5/server.py"},"output":"Wrote file successfully.","metadata":{"diagnostics":{},"filepath":"/Users/maui/.retort/work/retort-local-8zur77lj/retort-2e29d1db74f5/server.py","exists":false,"truncated":false},"title":"server.py","time":{"start":1788271740213,"end":1788271740216}},"metadata":{"openrouter":{"reasoning_details":[]}},"id":"prt_05d4d4533001gpCxA1rglZY46h","sessionID":"ses_fa2db0ef4ffeemTLK4uNaaAd5c","messageID":"msg_05d4d20f3001ZzIs8sDr0GEJy4"}}
