{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1788271799305,"sessionID":"ses_fa2db0ef4ffeemTLK4uNaaAd5c","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"bash","callID":"call_418bac206204414ea0c45d1c","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"command":"venv/bin/python - <<'EOF'\nfrom brazilian_soccer_mcp.dataset import load_dataset\nfrom brazilian_soccer_mcp import service as svc\nds = load_dataset()\n\nprint(\"== biggest wins overall ==\")\nbw = svc.biggest_wins(ds, limit=5)\nfor m in bw[\"matches\"]: print(\"  \", m[\"date\"], m[\"home_team\"], m[\"score\"], m[\"away_team\"], m[\"competition\"], m[\"season\"], \"margin\", m[\"margin\"])\nprint(\"== biggest wins Serie A ==\")\nbw = svc.biggest_wins(ds, competition=\"Brasileirão Serie A\", limit=3)\nfor m in bw[\"matches\"]: print(\"  \", m[\"date\"], m[\"home_team\"], m[\"score\"], m[\"away_team\"], m[\"season\"], \"margin\", m[\"margin\"])\n\nprint(\"== Palmeiras 2023 search ==\")\nr = svc.search_matches(ds, team=\"Palmeiras\", season=2023)\nprint(\"  total:\", r[\"total_matches\"], \"first:\", r[\"matches\"][0][\"date\"] if r[\"matches\"] else None)\n\nprint(\"== Palmeiras record 2023 ==\")\ntr = svc.team_record(ds, \"Palmeiras\", competition=\"serie a\", season=2023)\nprint(\"  \", tr[\"overall\"], tr[\"notes\"])\n\nprint(\"== list teams 2019 serie A ==\")\nlt = svc.list_teams(ds, \"Brasileirão Serie A\", 2019)\nprint(\"  count:\", lt[\"team_count\"])\n\nprint(\"== match statistics Flamengo 2023 ==\")\nms = svc.match_statistics(ds, team=\"Flamengo\", season=2023, limit=2)\nprint(\"  total:\", ms[\"total_matches\"], \"sample:\", ms[\"matches\"][0][\"statistics\"] if ms[\"matches\"] else None)\n\nprint(\"== competition info Libertadores seasons ==\")\nci = svc.competition_info(ds, \"libertadores\")\nfor s in ci[\"competitions\"][\"Copa Libertadores\"][\"seasons\"][:3]: print(\"  \", s[\"season\"], s[\"matches\"], s[\"champion\"], s.get(\"note\"))\n\nprint(\"== resolve Atletico Paranaense / America ==\")\nprint(\"  \", [(c[\"club\"], c[\"club_id\"]) for c in svc.resolve_team_info(ds, \"Atletico Paranaense\")[\"matches\"]])\nprint(\"  \", [(c[\"club\"], c[\"club_id\"]) for c in svc.resolve_team_info(ds, \"América\")[\"matches\"]])\nprint(\"  \", [(c[\"club\"], c[\"club_id\"]) for c in svc.resolve_team_info(ds, \"Boavista\")[\"matches\"]][:3])\n\nprint(\"== search Flamengo Fluminense ==\")\nr = svc.search_matches(ds, team=\"Flamengo\", opponent=\"Fluminense\")\nprint(\"  total:\", r[\"total_matches\"])\n\nprint(\"== bracket lib 2018 ==\")\nbr = svc.bracket(ds, \"libertadores\", 2018)\nprint(\"  rounds:\", [(x[\"round\"], len(x[\"matches\"])) for x in br[\"rounds\"]], \"group:\", br[\"group_stage_matches\"])\n\nprint(\"== fifa Alisson ==\")\nr = svc.find_players(ds, name=\"Alisson\")\nprint(\"  \", [(p[\"name\"], p[\"overall\"], p[\"club\"], p[\"position\"]) for p in r[\"players\"][:3]])\nr = svc.find_players(ds, nationality=\"Brazil\", position=\"forward\", min_overall=85)\nprint(\"  brazilians fwd >=85:\", [(p[\"name\"], p[\"overall\"]) for p in r[\"players\"]])\nEOF"},"output":"== biggest wins overall ==\n   2021-06-08 São Paulo 9-1 4 de Julho - PI Copa do Brasil 2021 margin 8\n   2017-09-21 River Plate 8-0 Jorge Wilstermann Copa Libertadores 2017 margin 8\n   2020-03-11 River Plate 8-0 Binacional Copa Libertadores 2020 margin 8\n   2017-09-09 Joinville 8-1 Mogi Mirim Brasileirão Serie C 2017 margin 7\n   2020-11-28 Brusque 1-8 Volta Redonda Brasileirão Serie C 2020 margin 7\n== biggest wins Serie A ==\n   2003-04-27 Goiás 7-0 Juventude 2003 margin 7\n   2003-12-14 Bahia 0-7 Cruzeiro 2003 margin 7\n   2004-09-28 São Paulo 7-0 Paysandu 2004 margin 7\n== Palmeiras 2023 search ==\n  total: 43 first: 2023-04-13\n== Palmeiras record 2023 ==\n   {'matches': 37, 'wins': 19, 'draws': 10, 'losses': 8, 'goals_for': 61, 'goals_against': 32, 'win_rate': 51.4} ['Data incomplete: only 37 of ~38 expected matches have scores in the source data.']\n== list teams 2019 serie A ==\n  count: 20\n== match statistics Flamengo 2023 ==\n  total: 48 sample: {'kickoff_time': '00:00:00', 'corners': '2-7', 'shots': '14-17', 'attacks': '121-126', 'half_time': 'WON'}\n== competition info Libertadores seasons ==\n   2013 126 None Aggregate tied 2-2 over the final; the winner was decided on penalties, which the dataset does not record.\n   2014 126 San Lorenzo None\n   2015 126 River Plate None\n== resolve Atletico Paranaense / America ==\n   [('Athletico Paranaense', 'atletico|PR')]\n   [('América Mineiro', 'america|MG'), ('America RN', 'america|RN')]\n   [('Boavista - RJ', 'boavista|RJ')]\n== search Flamengo Fluminense ==\n  total: 44\n== bracket lib 2018 ==\n  rounds: [('Final', 2), ('Semifinals', 4), ('Quarterfinals', 8), ('Round Of 16', 16)] group: 96\n== fifa Alisson ==\n   [('Alisson', 85, 'Liverpool', 'GK')]\n  brazilians fwd >=85: [('Neymar Jr', 92), ('Coutinho', 88)]\n","metadata":{"output":"== biggest wins overall ==\n   2021-06-08 São Paulo 9-1 4 de Julho - PI Copa do Brasil 2021 margin 8\n   2017-09-21 River Plate 8-0 Jorge Wilstermann Copa Libertadores 2017 margin 8\n   2020-03-11 River Plate 8-0 Binacional Copa Libertadores 2020 margin 8\n   2017-09-09 Joinville 8-1 Mogi Mirim Brasileirão Serie C 2017 margin 7\n   2020-11-28 Brusque 1-8 Volta Redonda Brasileirão Serie C 2020 margin 7\n== biggest wins Serie A ==\n   2003-04-27 Goiás 7-0 Juventude 2003 margin 7\n   2003-12-14 Bahia 0-7 Cruzeiro 2003 margin 7\n   2004-09-28 São Paulo 7-0 Paysandu 2004 margin 7\n== Palmeiras 2023 search ==\n  total: 43 first: 2023-04-13\n== Palmeiras record 2023 ==\n   {'matches': 37, 'wins': 19, 'draws': 10, 'losses': 8, 'goals_for': 61, 'goals_against': 32, 'win_rate': 51.4} ['Data incomplete: only 37 of ~38 expected matches have scores in the source data.']\n== list teams 2019 serie A ==\n  count: 20\n== match statistics Flamengo 2023 ==\n  total: 48 sample: {'kickoff_time': '00:00:00', 'corners': '2-7', 'shots': '14-17', 'attacks': '121-126', 'half_time': 'WON'}\n== competition info Libertadores seasons ==\n   2013 126 None Aggregate tied 2-2 over the final; the winner was decided on penalties, which the dataset does not record.\n   2014 126 San Lorenzo None\n   2015 126 River Plate None\n== resolve Atletico Paranaense / America ==\n   [('Athletico Paranaense', 'atletico|PR')]\n   [('América Mineiro', 'america|MG'), ('America RN', 'america|RN')]\n   [('Boavista - RJ', 'boavista|RJ')]\n== search Flamengo Fluminense ==\n  total: 44\n== bracket lib 2018 ==\n  rounds: [('Final', 2), ('Semifinals', 4), ('Quarterfinals', 8), ('Round Of 16', 16)] group: 96\n== fifa Alisson ==\n   [('Alisson', 85, 'Liverpool', 'GK')]\n  brazilians fwd >=85: [('Neymar Jr', 92), ('Coutinho', 88)]\n","exit":0,"truncated":false},"title":"venv/bin/python - <<'EOF'\nfrom brazilian_soccer_mcp.dataset import load_dataset\nfrom brazilian_soccer_mcp import service as svc\nds = load_dataset()\n\nprint(\"== biggest wins overall ==\")\nbw = svc.biggest_wins(ds, limit=5)\nfor m in bw[\"matches\"]: print(\"  \", m[\"date\"], m[\"home_team\"], m[\"score\"], m[\"away_team\"], m[\"competition\"], m[\"season\"], \"margin\", m[\"margin\"])\nprint(\"== biggest wins Serie A ==\")\nbw = svc.biggest_wins(ds, competition=\"Brasileirão Serie A\", limit=3)\nfor m in bw[\"matches\"]: print(\"  \", m[\"date\"], m[\"home_team\"], m[\"score\"], m[\"away_team\"], m[\"season\"], \"margin\", m[\"margin\"])\n\nprint(\"== Palmeiras 2023 search ==\")\nr = svc.search_matches(ds, team=\"Palmeiras\", season=2023)\nprint(\"  total:\", r[\"total_matches\"], \"first:\", r[\"matches\"][0][\"date\"] if r[\"matches\"] else None)\n\nprint(\"== Palmeiras record 2023 ==\")\ntr = svc.team_record(ds, \"Palmeiras\", competition=\"serie a\", season=2023)\nprint(\"  \", tr[\"overall\"], tr[\"notes\"])\n\nprint(\"== list teams 2019 serie A ==\")\nlt = svc.list_teams(ds, \"Brasileirão Serie A\", 2019)\nprint(\"  count:\", lt[\"team_count\"])\n\nprint(\"== match statistics Flamengo 2023 ==\")\nms = svc.match_statistics(ds, team=\"Flamengo\", season=2023, limit=2)\nprint(\"  total:\", ms[\"total_matches\"], \"sample:\", ms[\"matches\"][0][\"statistics\"] if ms[\"matches\"] else None)\n\nprint(\"== competition info Libertadores seasons ==\")\nci = svc.competition_info(ds, \"libertadores\")\nfor s in ci[\"competitions\"][\"Copa Libertadores\"][\"seasons\"][:3]: print(\"  \", s[\"season\"], s[\"matches\"], s[\"champion\"], s.get(\"note\"))\n\nprint(\"== resolve Atletico Paranaense / America ==\")\nprint(\"  \", [(c[\"club\"], c[\"club_id\"]) for c in svc.resolve_team_info(ds, \"Atletico Paranaense\")[\"matches\"]])\nprint(\"  \", [(c[\"club\"], c[\"club_id\"]) for c in svc.resolve_team_info(ds, \"América\")[\"matches\"]])\nprint(\"  \", [(c[\"club\"], c[\"club_id\"]) for c in svc.resolve_team_info(ds, \"Boavista\")[\"matches\"]][:3])\n\nprint(\"== search Flamengo Fluminense ==\")\nr = svc.search_matches(ds, team=\"Flamengo\", opponent=\"Fluminense\")\nprint(\"  total:\", r[\"total_matches\"])\n\nprint(\"== bracket lib 2018 ==\")\nbr = svc.bracket(ds, \"libertadores\", 2018)\nprint(\"  rounds:\", [(x[\"round\"], len(x[\"matches\"])) for x in br[\"rounds\"]], \"group:\", br[\"group_stage_matches\"])\n\nprint(\"== fifa Alisson ==\")\nr = svc.find_players(ds, name=\"Alisson\")\nprint(\"  \", [(p[\"name\"], p[\"overall\"], p[\"club\"], p[\"position\"]) for p in r[\"players\"][:3]])\nr = svc.find_players(ds, nationality=\"Brazil\", position=\"forward\", min_overall=85)\nprint(\"  brazilians fwd >=85:\", [(p[\"name\"], p[\"overall\"]) for p in r[\"players\"]])\nEOF","time":{"start":1788271799258,"end":1788271799304}},"metadata":{"openrouter":{"reasoning_details":[{"type":"reasoning.text","text":"Now the test suite. BDD GWT-structured pytest. Structure:\n\ntests/\n  conftest.py — module-scoped `dataset` fixture + `svc` helpers\n  test_normalize.py\n  test_dataset.py\n  test_match_queries.py\n  test_team_queries.py\n  test_player_queries.py\n  test_competition_queries.py\n  test_statistics.py\n  test_server.py\n  features/\n    match_queries.feature\n    team_queries.feature\n    player_queries.feature\n    competition_queries.feature\n    statistics.feature\n\nGWT style: each test with docstring Gherkin-ish Given/When/Then, and names like `test_given_loaded_matches_when_search_flamengo_vs_fluminense_then_returns_fixtures_with_date_score_competition`.\n\nThe spec's exact Gherkin:\n```\nScenario: Find matches between two teams\n  Given the match data is loaded\n  When I search for matches between \"Flamengo\" and \"Fluminense\"\n  Then I should receive a list of matches\n  And each match should have date, scores, and competition\n\nScenario: Get team statistics\n  Given the match data is loaded\n  When I request statistics for \"Palmeiras\" in season \"2023\"\n  Then I should receive wins, losses, draws, and goals\n```\n\nI'll implement these two verbatim plus ~35 more scenarios covering the spec's example questions. Assertions based on verified data facts:\n\n- 2019 Serie A: Flamengo champion 90 pts, 28W 6D 4L, GF 86 GA 37\n- 2019 relegated: Cruzeiro, Chapecoense, CSA, Avaí\n- 2019 2nd Santos 74 (22W) vs 3rd Palmeiras 74 (21W) — tiebreaker by wins ✓\n- 2021 relegated: Grêmio, Bahia, Sport, Chapecoense\n- Libertadores 2019 champion Flamengo (2-1 vs River Plate)\n- Libertadores 2018 final: River Plate (aggregate 5-3... legs: Boca 2-2 River, River 3-1 Boca → River 5-3)\n- Copa do Brasil 2019 champion Athletico Paranaense (3-1 aggregate)\n- Copa do Brasil 2021: no final detectable (incomplete)\n- Fla-Flu h2h: 44 matches, 18-14-12, 60-48 goals\n- Corinthians 2022 home: 15 scored matches, 10W 4D 1L, 21GF 7GA + completeness note (19 expected)\n- Palmeiras 2023: P37 W19 D10 L8 67 GF61 (from table above)\n- FIFA: 827 Brazilians; Neymar Jr 92 top; Grêmio 20 players avg 73.3; Alisson at Liverpool 85\n- top Brazilian 3: Neymar 92, Casemiro 88, Coutinho 88 (order among 88s by name — Casemiro, Coutinho alphabetical)\n- Serie A 2019 averages: 2.31 goals/match, home win 48.4%\n- biggest wins: need known facts — let me compute the actual top margins before pinning assertions (Santos 8-0? not in data — Libertadores starts 2013. Let me check top margins in a scratch run and pin plausible ones).\n- last Flamengo x Corinthians: 2023-10-08 Corinthians 1-1 Flamengo\n- derbies 2023: Fla-Flu 4, Gre-Nal 2 etc.\n- search_matches Palmeiras 2023: count = 37 (P37 from standings; total fixtures 37 in data? P37 for Palmeiras — so 37 matches)\n- match_statistics: Flamengo 2023 corners present\n- 2003 season: 552 matches (24 teams)\n- resolve: \"Atletico Paranaense\" → club id atletico|PR; \"Athletico\" → atletico|PR; \"Vasco da Gama\" → vasco|RJ; \"América\" ambiguous → América Mineiro first; \"River Plate\" → Argentine club (id riverplate|, 91 matches, 25 players)\n- bracket Libertadores 2018: 4 knockout rounds present, final = River/Boca\n- bracket CdB 2019: Final round with 2 matches\n- standings errors for cups; champion 2023 incomplete note\n- all 6 CSVs loaded (file_stats)\n- canonical: no duplicate (comp, season, date, home, away) — verified 0\n- performance: search < 2s, standings < 5s\n\nServer tests:\n- build_server() → FastMCP with 17 tools (list via mcp.list_tools())\n- each tool JSON-serializable: call the underlying service functions through... FastMCP tools are registered with decorated functions; to call them I need access — the inner functions are stored in mcp._tool_manager... That's private API. Better: test service functions directly for JSON, and test the server via stdio JSON-RPC round-trip (spawn `python server.py`, send initialize + tools/list + tools/call search_matches, parse responses). Let me write the stdio test carefully:\n\n```python\nproc = subprocess.Popen([sys.executable, \"server.py\"], stdin=PIPE, stdout=PIPE, stderr=DEVNULL)\n# MCP protocol over stdio: newline-delimited? No — MCP stdio uses LSP-style Content-Length headers? Actually MCP stdio transport uses newline-delimited JSON (JSON-RPC messages, one per line). Let me check the mcp python SDK: mcp.server.stdio uses anyio... The stdio server reads newline-delimited JSON-RPC messages. Yes — MCP stdio = newline-delimited JSON.\nsend: {\"jsonrpc\":\"2.0\",\"id\":1,\"method\":\"initialize\",\"params\":{\"protocolVersion\":\"2024-11-05\",\"capabilities\":{},\"clientInfo\":{\"name\":\"test\",\"version\":\"1.0\"}}}\nthen notification {\"jsonrpc\":\"2.0\",\"method\":\"notifications/initialized\"}\nthen {\"jsonrpc\":\"2.0\",\"id\":2,\"method\":\"tools/list\"}\nthen {\"jsonrpc\":\"2.0\",\"id\":3,\"method\":\"tools/call\",\"params\":{\"name\":\"resolve_team\",\"arguments\":{\"name\":\"Flamengo\"}}}\nread lines, parse.\n```\n\nprotocolVersion: the SDK mcp 2.1.1 — I'll echo the server's version from initialize result. Actually simpler: send a version string; the SDK accepts whatever. Let me be careful with read timing: read lines with a timeout via select or just blocking readline with the subprocess kept alive. Blocking readline could hang forever on failure — use a helper thread with timeout, or use `select.select` on POSIX. I'll write a helper `_read_rpc_line(proc, timeout)` using selectors on POSIX (we're on macOS ✓ tests run here). Add generous 60s for first call (dataset load ~1-3s).\n\nWait — one thing to check: does FastMCP's stdio write LSP-style \"Content-Length\" headers or newline JSON? In the MCP spec, stdio transport messages are newline-delimited JSON-RPC. The python SDK `mcp.server.stdio.stdio_server` reads lines. ✓.\n\nAlso the venv python is at venv/bin/python — sys.executable in tests = venv/bin/python ✓. cwd for subprocess: repo root — server.py imports brazilian_soccer_mcp → needs cwd on sys.path. When running `python server.py`, script dir = cwd automatically on sys.path ✓ (script's directory is added). ✓\n\nDataset default path: DATA_DIR_DEFAULT = parent of package dir / data / kaggle → repo/data/kaggle ✓ regardless of cwd.\n\nNow — timing: module-scoped fixture loads dataset once (~2-4s). Fine.\n\nAlso — before writing tests, let me pin the actual expected values with a scratch run (biggest wins, Palmeiras 2023 search count, match_statistics sample, list_teams 2019 count, competition_info structure, top scorers of goals etc.).","format":"unknown","index":0}]}},"id":"prt_05d4e2802001DEwrTLGukLUjcB","sessionID":"ses_fa2db0ef4ffeemTLK4uNaaAd5c","messageID":"msg_05d4d7c09001h95P3OsJc6Meng"}}
