{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1788271823979,"sessionID":"ses_fa2db0ef4ffeemTLK4uNaaAd5c","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"write","callID":"call_ee2029ebad884db2ada41e08","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"content":"\"\"\"\nShared pytest fixtures for the Brazilian Soccer MCP test suite.\n\nContext block\n-------------\nWhy:\n    Loading the six CSVs takes a couple of seconds; BDD scenarios across\n    six test modules must share one ``Dataset`` instance (and its cached\n    club registry) both for speed and for consistent expectations.\n\nWhat:\n    * ``dataset``     - module-scoped, loads the bundled Kaggle data once.\n    * ``svc``         - the service module (pure functions over ``dataset``).\n    * ``service``     - alias of ``svc`` for readable Given-steps.\n\nTest:\n    This file is fixtures-only; scenario suites live in\n    ``tests/test_*.py`` and their Gherkin counterparts in\n    ``tests/features/*.feature``.\n\nSpec references:\n    TASK.md \"Testing Approach\" (BDD / GWT structure) and \"Success\n    Criteria\" -> \"Query Performance\" (fixtures enable the <2s / <5s\n    assertions in ``tests/test_statistics.py``).\n\"\"\"\n\nfrom __future__ import annotations\n\nimport sys\nfrom pathlib import Path\n\nimport pytest\n\n# Make the repository root importable regardless of where pytest runs from.\nROOT = Path(__file__).resolve().parent.parent\nif str(ROOT) not in sys.path:\n    sys.path.insert(0, str(ROOT))\n\nfrom brazilian_soccer_mcp import service  # noqa: E402\nfrom brazilian_soccer_mcp.dataset import Dataset, load_dataset  # noqa: E402\n\n\n@pytest.fixture(scope=\"session\")\ndef dataset() -> Dataset:\n    \"\"\"The assembled knowledge base, loaded once per test session.\"\"\"\n    return load_dataset(ROOT / \"data\" / \"kaggle\")\n\n\n@pytest.fixture(scope=\"session\")\ndef svc() -> object:\n    \"\"\"The service module (query API) for When-steps.\"\"\"\n    return service\n","filePath":"/Users/maui/.retort/work/retort-local-8zur77lj/retort-2e29d1db74f5/tests/conftest.py"},"output":"Wrote file successfully.","metadata":{"diagnostics":{},"filepath":"/Users/maui/.retort/work/retort-local-8zur77lj/retort-2e29d1db74f5/tests/conftest.py","exists":false,"truncated":false},"title":"tests/conftest.py","time":{"start":1788271823975,"end":1788271823978}},"metadata":{"openrouter":{"reasoning_details":[{"type":"reasoning.text","text":"All values pinned. Interesting notes:\n1. \"Palmeiras 2023 search total: 43\" — 37 Serie A + 6 other (Copa do Brasil 2023, Libertadores 2023). ✓\n2. match_statistics Flamengo 2023: 48 rows (brf raw, includes dupes possibly — 38 Serie A + CdB/Lib legs) ✓ stats present ✓.\n3. Boavista resolves to \"Boavista - RJ\" (the Cup spelling as display since FIFA \"Boavista FC\" has 8 players vs Cup matches... the RJ club display fell back to most-common variant \"Boavista - RJ\"). Fine.\n4. bracket Lib 2018: \"Round Of 16\" title-cased oddly but fine.\n\nAlso note Libertadores 2013 champion: None (aggregate 2-2, penalties note) ✓ — and real winner was Atlético-MG on penalties. Good honest output.\n\nHmm — one thing: Palmeiras 2023 record shows \"37 of ~38\" note ✓.\n\nAlso `team_record(ds, \"Palmeiras\", competition=\"serie a\", ...)` — competition resolved from \"serie a\" ✓ works.\n\nNow — the FIFA \"Alisson 85 Liverpool\" — spec example says 89; data vintage differs; fine.\n\nOne more consideration — **search_matches for \"Flamengo vs Fluminense\" 2023-10-08 \"last Flamengo vs Corinthians: Corinthians 1-1 Flamengo\"** ✓ pinned earlier.\n\nNow let me also double-check the two Gherkin scenarios from the spec verbatim:\n1. \"search matches between Flamengo and Fluminense → list with date, scores, competition\" ✓ (44 matches)\n2. \"statistics for Palmeiras in season 2023 → wins, losses, draws, goals\" ✓ (19/8/10, 61/32)\n\nNow write the tests. conftest.py with module-scoped dataset fixture. Plus features/*.feature files. Let me write all test files now.\n\nTest count target: 20+ sample questions answerable — my test suite will cover ~40 scenarios. \n\nOne caution: tests use the venv python (pytest 9.1.1). Also test_server.py subprocess test: the `mcp` package must be importable by `python server.py` — venv ✓.\n\nFor the perf test: assert search < 2s and standings < 5s (warm). On this machine: dataset load ~3s (module fixture, one-time), queries ms. ✓ generous.\n\nEdge: pytest 9 — `tmp_path` etc fine. I'll avoid pytest-bdd.\n\nLet me write conftest and the test files.","format":"unknown","index":0}]}},"id":"prt_05d4e8c640015hEwq9KlK7xtgm","sessionID":"ses_fa2db0ef4ffeemTLK4uNaaAd5c","messageID":"msg_05d4e2d8900104Yn8PJryNZ6zk"}}
