 double-RR (22×21=462). Serie B 2022 real: 20 teams, 380 matches. The data has 380 matches + 22 teams = 2 bogus teams with few matches (GE Bage, Monsoon FC). Let me check their match counts — probably 1-2 matches each (data corruption). My test: assert team_count == 22 (data truth) OR make it robust: assert team_count >= 20 and top teams have 38 matches. I'll assert: table[0] has 38 matches and champion == \"Cruzeiro\" (real 2022 Serie B champion was Cruzeiro!). Let me verify quickly then pin.\n\n4. **Palmeiras seasons[0] == 2004** ✓ (relegated in 2003 to Serie B — real).\n\n5. **Libertadores unscored: 2 rows** — Boca x River 2015-05-14 (the famous abandoned match! Suspended at 0-0 — real historical event ✓) + the NA final row. → averages matches == 1253 ✓. Also finals count 15 ✓ (2+2+2+2+2+2+1+1 = 14 scored + 1 unscored NA... wait: finals list earlier: 2013×2, 2014×2, 2015×2, 2016×2, 2017×2, 2018×2, 2019×1, 2020×1, NA×1 = 15 ✓.\n\n6. **Real Madrid resolves via FIFA club** → my \"unknown team\" test should use a name that matches nothing: e.g. \"Honolulu United\" (base \"honoluluunited\", no containment match). And add a test that Real Madrid (valid club, no matches) returns empty matches gracefully.\n\n7. **Sport Recife fifa_source_club_name** — fix service: derive from players' raw club strings instead of variants[0].\n\n8. **bracket round ordering bug** — fix the label/sort logic.\n\n9. **team_profile fifa note** — use top-level \"note\".\n\nLet me fix service (bracket ordering, fifa_source_club_name) and the tests.","format":"unknown","index":0}]}},"id":"prt_05d56f8ea001QzrgWpSZyuYgh0","sessionID":"ses_fa2db0ef4ffeemTLK4uNaaAd5c","messageID":"msg_05d568592001m7u7qJjwhzKLoZ"}}
