ervice.py is defined after use but that's fine.\n\nOne more check — the stdio server subprocess test relies on `mcp` v2 behavior of `run()`. It passed ✓ (test_server passed).\n\nLet me also do a broader end-to-end smoke: run several tools through an actual MCP client-like session to make sure no serialization issues with edge outputs (e.g. standings with venue, resolve_team, error paths produce clean errors).","format":"unknown","index":0}]}},"id":"prt_05d5c2858001yKe9hv7H9hwcqW","sessionID":"ses_fa2db0ef4ffeemTLK4uNaaAd5c","messageID":"msg_05d5bf01e001mtj3wXz7eaYTXN"}}
