c.terminate(); proc.wait()\nprint(\"SMOKE OK\")\nEOF","timeout":180000},"output":"19 cup standings error -> Error executing tool standings\n20 Vasco profile -> [2018]\n21 unknown team error -> Error executing tool search_matches\n22 bad season error -> Error executing tool standings: 1 validation error for stand\nSMOKE OK\n","metadata":{"output":"19 cup standings error -> Error executing tool standings\n20 Vasco profile -> [2018]\n21 unknown team error -> Error executing tool search_matches\n22 bad season error -> Error executing tool standings: 1 validation error for stand\nSMOKE OK\n","exit":0,"truncated":false},"title":"venv/bin/python - <<'EOF'\nimport json, subprocess, sys, selectors, os\n\nproc = subprocess.Popen([sys.executable, \"server.py\"], stdin=subprocess.PIPE,\n                        stdout=subprocess.PIPE, stderr=subprocess.DEVNULL, text=True, bufsize=1,\n                        env=dict(os.environ, PYTHONUNBUFFERED=\"1\"))\nsel = selectors.DefaultSelector(); sel.register(proc.stdout, selectors.EVENT_READ)\ndef send(msg): proc.stdin.write(json.dumps(msg)+\"\\n\"); proc.stdin.flush()\ndef recv(timeout=60):\n    while True:\n        if not sel.select(timeout): raise TimeoutError\n        line = proc.stdout.readline()\n        if line.strip(): return json.loads(line)\ndef call(i, name, args):\n    send({\"jsonrpc\":\"2.0\",\"id\":i,\"method\":\"tools/call\",\"params\":{\"name\":name,\"arguments\":args}})\n    r = recv(); assert r[\"id\"] == i, r\n    text = r[\"result\"][\"content\"][0][\"text\"]\n    if r[\"result\"].get(\"isError\"):\n        return {\"_error\": text}\n    return json.loads(text)\n\nsend({\"jsonrpc\":\"2.0\",\"id\":1,\"method\":\"initialize\",\"params\":{\"protocolVersion\":\"2024-11-05\",\"capabilities\":{},\"clientInfo\":{\"name\":\"smoke\",\"version\":\"1\"}}}); recv()\nsend({\"jsonrpc\":\"2.0\",\"method\":\"notifications/initialized\"})\n\nprint(\"19 cup standings error ->\", call(20,\"standings\",{\"competition\":\"Copa do Brasil\",\"season\":2019})[\"_error\"][:80])\nprint(\"20 Vasco profile ->\", call(21,\"team_profile\",{\"team\":\"Vasco\"})[\"competitions\"][\"Copa Libertadores\"][\"seasons\"][:3])\nprint(\"21 unknown team error ->\", call(22,\"search_matches\",{\"team\":\"ZZZ Bogus\"})[\"_error\"][:60])\nprint(\"22 bad season error ->\", call(23,\"standings\",{\"competition\":\"serie a\",\"season\":\"abc\"})[\"_error\"][:60])\nproc.terminate(); proc.wait()\nprint(\"SMOKE OK\")\nEOF","time":{"start":1788272776173,"end":1788272776177}},"metadata":{"openrouter":{"reasoning_details":[{"type":"reasoning.text","text":"The 2017 CdB final in the data: Flamengo 1-1 Cruzeiro, then Cruzeiro 0-0 Flamengo → aggregate 1-1. The REAL 2017 final: first leg Flamengo 1-1 Cruzeiro? Hmm — actually I recall the second leg was 0-0 and Cruzeiro won... wait, real 2017: leg 1 at Maracanã: Flamengo 1-1 Cruzeiro? and leg 2 Mineirão: Cruzeiro 0-0 Flamengo → 1-1 aggregate, Cruzeiro won ON PENALTIES?? Hmm — no. Let me think: 2017 Copa do Brasil final — Cruzeiro beat Flamengo. I believe leg 1: Flamengo 1-1? Hmm... Actually I remember leg 2 was 0-0 at Mineirão and Cruzeiro won the title. If aggregate was 1-1, penalties decided it (Cruzeiro won on penalties? no — hmm, I genuinely recall \"Cruzeiro campeão da Copa do Brasil 2017\" with a 0-0 second leg). Real fact-check: 2017 CdB final first leg (Sep 7): Flamengo 1-1 Cruzeiro? Hmm — no wait, I think first leg was Flamengo 1-1? Hmm. If so aggregate 1-1 → penalties → Cruzeiro champion. Hmm, but I also vaguely remember \"Cruzeiro 3-1 aggregate\"? That might be 2018 (Cruzeiro beat Corinthians in 2018 final 3-1 aggregate ✓ — 2018: Corinthians 1-2? leg1 1-1, leg2 0-2? whatever).\n\nSo 2017 per data: 1-1 aggregate, penalties → the honest \"winner not determinable\" answer ✓ CORRECT behavior (Cruzeiro won on penalties in reality). My smoke expectation of a name was wrong, not the code.\n\nNow fix the smoke script to handle error results properly and re-run to confirm #19/#20.",