{"type":"text","timestamp":1788272975593,"sessionID":"ses_fa2db0ef4ffeemTLK4uNaaAd5c","part":{"id":"prt_05d6006d9001fRZRbCLH0a2MB0","messageID":"msg_05d5fbf3a001Bis1RbULZyjy0V","sessionID":"ses_fa2db0ef4ffeemTLK4uNaaAd5c","type":"text","text":"Everything complete. Final state:\n\n**Implementation** (all in the working directory):\n- `brazilian_soccer_mcp/` — `normalize.py` (accent folding, date formats, team aliases, competition resolution), `registry.py` (club knowledge graph: every spelling variant → one club entity, ambiguity surfaced), `dataset.py` (loads all 6 CSVs, builds a deduplicated canonical index), `service.py` (all query logic), `server.py` (FastMCP wiring, mcp v1/v2 compatible), `models.py`\n- `server.py` + `pyproject.toml` — stdio entry point and `brazilian-soccer-mcp` console script\n- `tests/` — **126 BDD GWT scenarios passing in ~3s**, plus Gherkin `.feature` counterparts in `tests/features/`\n\n**Key design decisions** (validated against real history in tests):\n- **One authoritative source per (competition, season)** — the five match files overlap and disagree on dates (~10%), so per-season source selection is the only safe dedup: novo 2003-11, dedicated files 2012-22, BR-Football 2023\n- **Honest data gaps** — unscored \"NA\" rows excluded from stats; standings flag incompleteness (2023: 377/380); penalty-decided finals report \"not determinable\"; missing FIFA rosters (Flamengo, Palmeiras...) are noted, not errored\n- **Verified accuracy**: 2019 Flamengo 90 pts champion with the wins tiebreaker (Santos > Palmeiras at 74), 2019/2020/2021 relegation zones, 2022 Série B Cruzeiro, Libertadores 2018/2019 winners, 2017 CdB 1-1 aggregate → penalties note\n\n**Checks**: `pytest` 126 passed · `ruff check` + `format` clean · full stdio JSON-RPC round trip with actionable error messages verified live.","time":{"start":1788272969433,"end":1788272975592}}}
